#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid "broken console"
msgstr "壊れたコンソール"

#. ~ Description of furniture "broken console"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid ""
"A standalone computer terminal.  It doesn't seem to be working.  It's the "
"broken screen and shattered circuit boards telling you that."
msgstr "スタンドアロン型のコンピュータ端末です。正常に機能していないことは、割れたスクリーンと粉々になった回路基板を見れば明白です。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid "computer console"
msgstr "コンピュータコンソール"

#. ~ Description of furniture "computer console"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid ""
"A standalone computer terminal, the screen glowing with dim artificial "
"light.  If examined closely, you can read what's on the screen and perform "
"any allowed functions.  It might even be possible to hack it, given the "
"skills."
msgstr ""
"モニタから薄暗い人工光を発している、スタンドアロン型のコンピュータ端末です。調べることで、モニタに表示されている表示内容を読み、操作を実行できます。技術さえあれば、ハッキングもできるかもしれません。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Blueprint name of recipe crafting "fbmw_2_common_1"
#. ~ Blueprint name of recipe crafting "fbmw_2_common_smithy_2"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#: data/json/recipes/basecamps/expansion/recipe_modular_workshop/version_2/recipe_modular_workshop_common.json
msgid "forge"
msgstr "炉"

#. ~ Description of furniture "forge"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid "A metalworking station typically used in combination with an anvil."
msgstr "金床と共に使うのが一般的な、金属加工設備です。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid "Cody's forge"
msgstr "コディの炉"

#. ~ Description of furniture "Cody's forge"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid ""
"A metalworking station typically used in combination with an anvil.  You can"
" see pipes running into the walls."
msgstr "金床と共に使うのが一般的な金属加工設備です。本体からパイプが伸び、壁の中へ続いています。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "anvil"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid ""
"A heavy block of oddly-shaped metal with a pritchel hole and hardy hole.  "
"It's used for metalworking."
msgstr "丸い穴と四角い穴が開いた、奇妙な形状の非常に重い金属の塊です。 金属加工に用いられます。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid "bronze anvil"
msgid_plural "bronze anvils"
msgstr[0] "金床(青銅)"

#. ~ Description of furniture "bronze anvil"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid ""
"A heavy block of oddly-shaped bronze with a pritchel hole and hardy hole.  "
"It's used for metalworking."
msgstr "丸い穴と四角い穴が開いた、奇妙な形状の非常に重い青銅の塊です。 金属加工に用いられます。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#: data/json/items/fake.json data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid "heavy anvil"
msgid_plural "heavy anvils"
msgstr[0] "金床(巨大)"

#. ~ Description of furniture "heavy anvil"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid ""
"An enormously heavy block of oddly-shaped metal with all the accoutrements a"
" blacksmith could ask for.  It's used for heavy-duty metalworking."
msgstr "鍛冶屋が求めるあらゆる機能を備えた、奇妙な形状の非常に巨大な鋼鉄の塊です。大型の金属加工に用いられます。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid "crude anvil"
msgid_plural "crude anvils"
msgstr[0] "金床(粗製)"

#. ~ Description of furniture "crude anvil"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid ""
"A heavy anvil-shaped block of steel.  It's used for simple metalworking."
msgstr "金床の形に整えた重い鋼鉄の塊です。単純な金属加工に用いられます。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid "still"
msgid_plural "stills"
msgstr[0] "蒸留器"

#. ~ Description of furniture "still"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid ""
"An essential component for brewing and chemistry that allows for refining "
"liquid mixtures."
msgstr "混合した液体を精製する、醸造や化学実験に必要不可欠な道具です。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json data/json/items/tool/deployable.json
msgid "screw press"
msgid_plural "screw presses"
msgstr[0] "スクリュープレス"

#. ~ Description of furniture "screw press"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid ""
"A large screw press for manually pressing oil out of fruit or seed paste.  "
"The paste is placed in wetted bags and pressed down by the force of the "
"screw mechanism."
msgstr ""
"果実や種子のペーストを搾って油を採取するための、手動式の大型スクリュープレスです。湿らせた袋に入れたペーストを、ネジ機構で押し潰して搾ります。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid "charcoal kiln"
msgid_plural "charcoal kilns"
msgstr[0] "炭焼窯"

#. ~ Description of furniture "charcoal kiln"
#. ~ Description of furniture "filled charcoal kiln"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid ""
"A primitive rock kiln designed to burn wood and organic material into "
"charcoal in the absence of oxygen.  It isn't especially efficient compared "
"to a modern metal variant."
msgstr "木材や有機物を酸素のない状態で燃焼させて炭に加工する、原始的な窯です。現代の窯と比べると性能は高くありません。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
msgid "filled charcoal kiln"
msgid_plural "filled charcoal kilns"
msgstr[0] "炭焼窯(木材投入済)"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid "metal charcoal kiln"
msgstr "金属製炭焼窯"

#. ~ Description of furniture "metal charcoal kiln"
#. ~ Description of furniture "filled metal charcoal kiln"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid ""
"A metal kiln designed to burn wood and organic material into charcoal in the"
" absence of oxygen.  Much more efficient than its archaic rock counterpart."
msgstr "木材や有機物を酸素のない状態で燃焼させて炭に加工する、金属製の窯です。石を並べて作った昔ながらの窯より遥かに高性能です。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid "filled metal charcoal kiln"
msgstr "金属製炭焼窯(木材投入済)"

#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#: data/json/items/fake.json
msgid "arc furnace"
msgid_plural "arc furnaces"
msgstr[0] "アーク炉"

#. ~ Description of furniture "arc furnace"
#. ~ Description of furniture "filled arc furnace"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid ""
"An arc furnace designed to burn a powdery mix of coke and limestone to "
"create calcium carbide."
msgstr "アーク炉です。コークスと石灰石を混ぜた粉末を入れて燃焼すると、炭化カルシウムが生成できます。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid "filled arc furnace"
msgstr "アーク炉(装填済)"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid "smoking rack"
msgstr "燻製ラック"

#. ~ Description of furniture "smoking rack"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid ""
"A wooden rack designed to smoke food for better preservation and taste.  "
"Works as a charcoal smoker in crafting recipes."
msgstr "内部で食品を燻して日持ちと味を向上させる、木製のラックです。製作の際は燻製器として機能します。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#: data/json/items/fake.json
msgid "spinning wheel"
msgid_plural "spinning wheels"
msgstr[0] "糸車"

#. ~ Description of furniture "spinning wheel"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid ""
"A large wooden device with a mechanical wheel used to combine fibers "
"together into a stronger material."
msgstr "繊維をより合わせて強度を高めるために使う、木製のホイールが付いた大きな装置です。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#: data/json/items/fake.json
msgid "stationary scutcher"
msgid_plural "stationary scutchers"
msgstr[0] "打綿装置"

#. ~ Description of furniture "stationary scutcher"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid ""
"A bulky, simple-hinged wooden device to break up the hard parts of fiber "
"plants, with nail combs on the back for separating them out."
msgstr ""
"蝶番で留めた部品で植物の硬い繊維質を叩いてほぐす、シンプルな作りの大きな木製装置です。背面に櫛のように並んだ釘を使い、ほぐした繊維を梳いて選り分けます。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid "active smoking rack"
msgstr "燻製ラック(稼働)"

#. ~ Description of furniture "active smoking rack"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid ""
"A wooden rack designed to smoke food for better preservation and taste.  It "
"is lit and smoking."
msgstr "食品を燻して日持ちと味を向上させる木製のラックです。点火されており、内部で燻製が進行しています。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#: data/json/items/tool/deployable.json
msgid "metal smoking rack"
msgid_plural "metal smoking racks"
msgstr[0] "燻製ラック"

#. ~ Description of furniture "metal smoking rack"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid ""
"A metal rack designed to smoke food for better preservation and taste.  "
"Works as a charcoal smoker in crafting recipes."
msgstr "食品を燻して日持ちと味を向上させる金属製のラックです。製作の際は燻製器として機能します。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid "active metal smoking rack"
msgstr "折畳式燻製ラック(稼働)"

#. ~ Description of furniture "active metal smoking rack"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid "A metal rack designed to smoke food for better preservation and taste."
msgstr "食品を燻して日持ちと味を向上させる金属製のラックです。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid "rock forge"
msgstr "石炉"

#. ~ Description of furniture "rock forge"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid ""
"A metalworking station made of rock, typically used in combination with an "
"anvil.  Works as a charcoal forge in crafting recipes."
msgstr "金床と共に使うのが一般的な、石でできた金属加工設備です。製作の際は炭火炉として機能します。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid "clay kiln"
msgstr "陶芸窯"

#. ~ Description of furniture "clay kiln"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid "A kiln designed to bake clay pottery and bricks."
msgstr "陶器やレンガを焼くための窯です。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid "wooden stepladder"
msgid_plural "wooden stepladders"
msgstr[0] "脚立(木)"

#. ~ Description of furniture "wooden stepladder"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid ""
"A short, foldable wooden ladder.  Can help you climb to a rooftop, or maybe "
"slow something down."
msgstr "折り畳める木製の短い梯子です。屋上に登る際や、通行者の足止めをしたいときに役立ちます。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid "aluminum stepladder"
msgid_plural "aluminum stepladders"
msgstr[0] "脚立(アルミ)"

#. ~ Description of furniture "aluminum stepladder"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid ""
"A short, foldable aluminum ladder.  Can help you climb to a rooftop, or "
"maybe slow something down."
msgstr "折り畳めるアルミニウム製の短い梯子です。屋上に登る際や、通行者の足止めをしたいときに役立ちます。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#: data/json/items/fake.json
msgid "industrial arc furnace"
msgid_plural "industrial arc furnaces"
msgstr[0] "工業用アーク炉"

#. ~ Description of furniture "industrial arc furnace"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid ""
"Not the kind of furnace you'd heat your house with, this is a device for "
"heating things to extreme temperatures as part of industrial fabrication "
"processes.  Can be used in recipes instead of a forge, when supplied with "
"power from a UPS."
msgstr ""
"家庭用の暖房炉ではなく、工場などでの製造工程で素材を超高温に加熱するための装置です。UPSから電力を供給できれば、炉の代わりとして製作に利用できます。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#: data/json/items/fake.json data/json/items/tool/deployable.json
msgid "Beverly shear"
msgid_plural "Beverly shears"
msgstr[0] "レバーシャー"

#. ~ Description of furniture "Beverly shear"
#. ~ Description of "Beverly shear"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#: data/json/items/tool/deployable.json
msgid ""
"A massive bench-mounted device with a short guillotine blade mounted to a "
"long lever.  Designed for making straight or curved cuts through sheet metal"
" up to 3 millimeters thick."
msgstr "長いレバーの先に短い剪断刃が付いた、重量感のある卓上切断機です。厚さ3mmまでの板金を直線や曲線の形状に切断することができます。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "drill press"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid ""
"A powerful drill mounted on a slide that lets it drop precisely down.  "
"Useful in all kinds of projects from industrial fabrication to home "
"woodworking.  You can take this down and plug it into your own power grid to"
" use it."
msgstr ""
"正確な位置に穴を開けられる強力なドリルです。工業加工品から家庭の木工品まで、あらゆる製作の場面で役立ちます。電気配線と接続して使用できます。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid "firefly terrarium"
msgstr "生物発光灯"

#. ~ Description of furniture "firefly terrarium"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid ""
"While many survivors would have focused on trying to bring back electric "
"lights, whoever lives here has apparently decided to make use of the changes"
" wrought by the Cataclysm to provide light.  This vivarium contains soil, "
"strange plants you don't recognize immediately, and most strikingly, a giant"
" mutant firefly."
msgstr ""
"大抵の生存者は電気を使って照明を復旧しようとするものですが、ここの住人は、大変動による環境変化を利用して光源を確保することにしたようです。飼育容器の中には、土と見たこともない奇妙な植物、そして驚くべきことに、変異した巨大なホタルが入っています。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "table saw"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid ""
"A rotating sawblade set into a large, flat table, for making straight "
"measured cuts.  It's a key tool in any carpenter's arsenal.  You can take "
"this down and plug it into your own power grid to use it."
msgstr ""
"広く平らなテーブルに回転のこぎり刃が固定されており、まっすぐ正確に素材を切ることができます。取り外して任意の場所に移し、電気配線と接続して使用できます。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "mitre saw"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid ""
"A circular sawblade on an arm that can slide and rotate in several "
"directions, this is a staple tool for nearly any carpentry.  You can take "
"this down and plug it into your own power grid to use it."
msgstr ""
"大抵の木材加工をこなせる、角度を変えられるアームに丸ノコギリ刃が取り付けられた装置です。取り外して任意の場所に移し、電気配線と接続して使用できます。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "band saw"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid ""
"A ribbonlike sawblade runs in a single direction in this tool, allowing "
"precise cuts at almost any angle.  You can take this down and plug it into "
"your own power grid to use it."
msgstr ""
"帯状ののこぎり刃が一定方向に回転する工具です。さまざまな角度を付けて素材を正確に切断できます。取り外して任意の場所に移し、電気配線と接続して使用できます。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "router table"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid ""
"This table has an inset router, a rotating motor with an exchangeable blade "
"head for cutting specific profiles and grooves and stuff.  You can take this"
" down and plug it into your own power grid to use it."
msgstr ""
"交換可能なブレードを使って様々な素材の切断や溝彫りをこなすルーターが、テーブルに取り付けられています。取り外して任意の場所に移し、電気配線と接続して使用できます。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "planer"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid ""
"A hefty tool that will take in a board and cut it smooth and flat to a "
"specific width, particularly great if working with raw lumber stock, but "
"also good just for shaving wood down to size.  You can take this down and "
"plug it into your own power grid to use it."
msgstr ""
"大きな板材の平滑化や凹凸の研削を行なう大型機械です。特に生材の加工に適していますが、加工済みの木材のかんな掛けも得意です。取り外して任意の場所に移し、電気配線と接続して使用できます。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "jointer"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid ""
"A table-shaped tool with a rotating blade that will cut down, smooth out, "
"and square off a board to make it very smooth and nice indeed.  You can take"
" this down and plug it into your own power grid to use it."
msgstr ""
"回転する刃が付いたテーブルです。木材を切り分け、滑らかにし、四角形に切り落とす一連の作業を素早く正確にこなします。取り外して任意の場所に移し、電気配線と接続して使用できます。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid "disconnected catalytic cracking reactor"
msgstr "接触分解リアクター"

#. ~ Description of furniture "disconnected catalytic cracking reactor"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid ""
"A makeshift extraction system, or as makeshift as you can consider something"
" that was purpose-built in a laboratory by a group of experts.  You can take"
" this down and plug it into your own power grid to use it."
msgstr ""
"その場しのぎで作られた抽出装置ですが、専門家集団が実験室で自作したものと比べても遜色ありません。取り外して任意の場所に移し、電気配線と接続して使用できます。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "hydraulic press"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid ""
"If you really want to squash something a lot, this would be exactly the "
"right industrial tool for you.  You can take this down and plug it into your"
" own power grid to use it."
msgstr "何かを大量に潰したいと思っている人にうってつけの工業用機械です。取り外して任意の場所に移し、電気配線と接続して使用できます。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#: data/json/items/fake.json
msgid "power lathe"
msgid_plural "power lathes"
msgstr[0] "旋盤"

#. ~ Description of furniture "power lathe"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid ""
"An industrial-grade lathe, for turning chunks of metal and other hard things"
" into round chunks of metal and other hard things."
msgstr "金属などの硬い素材を回転させて加工する業務用旋盤です。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "air compressor"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid ""
"This durable tank is topped with a motor that will cram as much air into the"
" tank as possible.  You can take this down and plug it into your own power "
"grid to use it."
msgstr "大量の空気を吸入するモーターが搭載された、頑丈なタンクです。取り外して任意の場所に移し、電気配線と接続して使用できます。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#: data/json/items/tool/deployable.json
msgid "manual tire changer"
msgid_plural "manual tire changers"
msgstr[0] "手動タイヤチェンジャー"

#. ~ Description of furniture "manual tire changer"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid ""
"This floor-mounted machine contains all the levers, clamps and mounts "
"required to remove or fit a tire, plus an integrated foot pump to inflate "
"it."
msgstr "タイヤの着脱に必要なレバー、クランプ、マウントに加え、タイヤを加圧するための足踏み式ポンプも内蔵している、設置して使う機械です。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#: data/mods/innawood/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid "fermenting vat"
msgstr "発酵大桶"

#. ~ Description of furniture "fermenting vat"
#. ~ Description of furniture "filled fermenting vat"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid ""
"A sealable 50-liter vat for fermenting vinegar and various alcoholic brews."
msgstr "50Lの液体を密封できる、酢や酒を発酵させるための大桶です。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid "filled fermenting vat"
msgstr "発酵大桶(満)"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid "wooden fermenting vat"
msgstr "木製発酵大桶"

#. ~ Description of furniture "wooden fermenting vat"
#. ~ Description of furniture "filled wooden fermenting vat"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid ""
"A sealable 50-liter wooden vat for fermenting vinegar and various alcoholic "
"brews."
msgstr "50Lの液体を密封できる、酢や酒を発酵させるための木製大桶です。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid "filled wooden fermenting vat"
msgstr "木製発酵大桶(満)"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid "anaerobic digester"
msgstr "嫌気性消化槽"

#. ~ Description of furniture "anaerobic digester"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid "A 1000 L anaerobic digester."
msgstr "容量1000Lの嫌気性消化槽です。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid "filled anaerobic digester"
msgstr "嫌気性消化槽(満)"

#. ~ Description of furniture "filled anaerobic digester"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid "A 1000L anaerobic digester."
msgstr "容量1000Lの嫌気性消化槽です。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid "butchering rack"
msgstr "食肉処理ラック"

#. ~ Description of furniture "butchering rack"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid "A wooden butchering rack designed to hang a carcass in the air."
msgstr "枝肉を宙吊りにできる、木製の食肉処理ラックです。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#: data/json/items/tool/deployable.json
msgid "metal butchering rack"
msgid_plural "metal butchering racks"
msgstr[0] "食肉処理ラック"

#. ~ Description of furniture "metal butchering rack"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid ""
"A metal butchering rack designed to hang a carcass in the air.  It can be "
"deconstructed and folded for easy transportation."
msgstr "枝肉を宙吊りにできる、金属製の食肉処理ラックです。分解すれば簡単に持ち運べます。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid "hanging meathook"
msgstr "食肉用フック"

#. ~ Description of furniture "hanging meathook"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid "A hefty hook suspended from a chain for stringing up corpses."
msgstr "チェーンで吊り下げられた、死体を吊るすための大きなフックです。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#: data/json/items/tool/deployable.json
msgid "wind mill"
msgid_plural "wind mills"
msgstr[0] "粉挽き風車"

#. ~ Description of furniture "wind mill"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid ""
"A small wind-powered mill that can convert starchy products into flour."
msgstr "でんぷん質を含むアイテムを穀粉に加工する小型の風車です。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid "active wind mill"
msgstr "粉挽き風車(稼働)"

#. ~ Description of furniture "active wind mill"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid ""
"A small wind-powered mill that can convert starchy products into flour.  Its"
" brake has been removed and it is turning."
msgstr "でんぷん質を含むアイテムを穀粉に加工する小型の風車です。ブレーキ機構が解除され、回転しています。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#: data/json/items/tool/deployable.json
msgid "water mill"
msgid_plural "water mills"
msgstr[0] "粉挽き水車"

#. ~ Description of furniture "water mill"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid ""
"A small water-powered mill that can convert starchy products into flour."
msgstr "でんぷん質を含むアイテムを穀粉に加工する小型の水車です。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid "active water mill"
msgstr "粉挽き水車(稼働)"

#. ~ Description of furniture "active water mill"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid ""
"A small water-powered mill that can convert starchy products into flour.  "
"Its brake has been removed and it is turning."
msgstr "でんぷん質を含むアイテムを穀粉に加工する小型の水車です。ブレーキ機構が解除され、回転しています。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid "automated gas console"
msgstr "自動給油装置"

#. ~ Description of furniture "automated gas console"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid "An automated gas flow control console."
msgstr "自動でガソリン流量を制御する給油装置です。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid "broken automated gas console"
msgstr "壊れた自動給油装置"

#. ~ Description of furniture "broken automated gas console"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid ""
"An automated gas flow control console.  It's broken.  This is not a good "
"thing."
msgstr "自動でガソリン流量を制御する給油装置です。残念ながら壊れています。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid "reinforced vending machine"
msgstr "強化自動販売機"

#. ~ Description of furniture "reinforced vending machine"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid ""
"A bit tougher to crack open than a regular vending machine.  That just makes"
" it all the sweeter of a target, doesn't it?"
msgstr "通常のものと比べて略奪が多少困難な自動販売機です。だからこそ、狙ってみたくなりませんか？"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid "reinforced vending machine (off)"
msgstr "強化自動販売機(オフ)"

#. ~ Description of furniture "reinforced vending machine (off)"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid ""
"A bit tougher to crack open than a regular vending machine.  Out of order, "
"for lack of power.  That just makes it all the sweeter of a target, doesn't "
"it?"
msgstr "通常のものと比べて略奪が多少困難な自動販売機ですが、電力不足のため機能していません。だからこそ、狙ってみたくなりませんか？"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid "vending machine"
msgstr "自動販売機"

#. ~ Description of furniture "vending machine"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid ""
"An upright metal cabinet with a see-through door.  The goods inside can be "
"yours if you have money on a cash card."
msgstr "前面が透明なパネルで覆われた金属製キャビネットです。キャッシュカードに残金があれば、中の商品を購入できます。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid "vending machine (off)"
msgstr "自動販売機(オフ)"

#. ~ Description of furniture "vending machine (off)"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid ""
"An upright metal cabinet with a see-through door.  Out of order, for lack of"
" power."
msgstr "前面が透明なパネルで覆われた金属製キャビネットです。電力不足のため機能していません。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid "broken vending machine"
msgstr "壊れた自動販売機"

#. ~ Description of furniture "broken vending machine"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid ""
"An upright metal cabinet with a see-through door.  It's smashed open, so you"
" can take whatever you want for free."
msgstr "前面が透明なパネルで覆われた金属製キャビネットです。パネルがこじ開けられているため、商品がタダで手に入ります。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid "grappling hook"
msgid_plural "grappling hooks"
msgstr[0] "フック付きロープ"

#. ~ Description of furniture "grappling hook"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid ""
"A dangling piece of rope, hooked securely to something above you.  You could"
" climb up or take it down."
msgstr "もう一方を上部にしっかりと結びつけたロープが垂れ下がっています。上層や下層に移動できそうです。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid "vine leading up"
msgstr "上層に伸びた蔦"

#. ~ Description of furniture "vine leading up"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid ""
"A thick vine is rigidly anchored to something above you.  It looks quite "
"alive.  You could climb up or tear it down."
msgstr "まだ瑞々しい太い蔦が上層にしっかりと固定されています。上層に登るか、壊すことができます。"

#. ~ Bashing failed sound
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid "twang."
msgstr "ビヨン。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid "web leading up"
msgstr "上層に伸びたクモ糸"

#. ~ Description of furniture "web leading up"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid ""
"A thick, dangling strand of slightly sticky web, the other end is tied "
"securely to something above you.  You could use it to climb up."
msgstr "もう一方を上部にしっかりと結びつけた、少し粘つく太いクモ糸が垂れ下がっています。これを使えば上層に移動できそうです。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid "rope hoist"
msgstr "巻き上げ機(ロープ)"

#. ~ Description of furniture "rope hoist"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid ""
"A loop of rope hangs here, using a sturdy horizontal support as a basic "
"pulley.  While crude, it gives you some mechanical advantage for lifting "
"things."
msgstr ""
"地面と水平に伸びた頑丈な支柱を滑車代わりにして、ロープで作った輪がぶら下がっています。簡単な作りですが、力学的に荷物をある程度持ち上げやすくなる効果があります。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid "rope and tackle hoist"
msgstr "巻き上げ機(ロープ&滑車)"

#. ~ Description of furniture "rope and tackle hoist"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid ""
"A loop of rope hangs here, looped through a quality tackle to give a "
"significant mechanical advantage while lifting heavy objects."
msgstr "ロープで作った輪が、高品質の滑車にぶら下がっています。力学的に、重量物を非常に楽に持ち上げられるようになっています。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid "chain hoist"
msgstr "巻き上げ機(チェーン&滑車)"

#. ~ Description of furniture "chain hoist"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
msgid ""
"A sturdy chain and heavy tackle hang well-supported from the ceiling here, "
"ready to lift most heavy items you could think of using mechanical "
"advantage."
msgstr "天井に重厚な滑車が備わっており、そこから頑丈なチェーンがぶら下がっています。力学的に、どんな重い物でも持ち上げられるようになっています。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-triffid.json
msgid "illuminating plant bulb"
msgstr "光る球根"

#. ~ Description of furniture "illuminating plant bulb"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-triffid.json
msgid ""
"A small plant grows among the roots here, its green, onion-like bulb "
"illuminating the area around it."
msgstr "小さな植物が根を張っており、タマネギのような球根が周囲を照らしています。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-triffid.json
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/furniture_and_terrain/furniture.json
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-plants.json
msgid "brambles"
msgstr "絡み合った植物"

#. ~ Description of furniture "brambles"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-triffid.json
msgid ""
"A wall of tangled roots blocks the path here, you'd have destroy it to get "
"past."
msgstr "絡み合った根の壁が道を塞いでいます。破壊しなければ通り抜けられません。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-triffid.json
msgid "composting midden"
msgstr "堆肥"

#. ~ Description of furniture "composting midden"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-triffid.json
msgid ""
"A hole has been dug into the roots here, and a pretty unpleasant smell emits"
" from it."
msgstr "根元に掘られた穴の中から、非常に不快な臭いが漂ってきます。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_nether_monster.json
msgid "decaying tube"
msgstr "腐った肉柱"

#. ~ Description of furniture "decaying tube"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_nether_monster.json
msgid "A decomposing fleshy stalagmite extends from the ceiling to the floor."
msgstr "腐敗した肉が、鍾乳石のように天井から床に垂れ下がっています。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_nether_monster.json
msgid "glowing decaying tube"
msgstr "腐った発光肉柱"

#. ~ Description of furniture "glowing decaying tube"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_nether_monster.json
msgid ""
"A decomposing fleshy stalagmite extends from the ceiling to the floor.  "
"Countless glowing spores weft from within, coating everything nearby."
msgstr "腐敗した肉が、鍾乳石のように天井から床に垂れ下がっています。その内部から無数の光り輝く粒子が溢れ、周囲に降り積もっています。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_nether_monster.json
msgid "beautiful nether lily"
msgstr "異界のユリ"

#. ~ Description of furniture "beautiful nether lily"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_nether_monster.json
msgid ""
"A very tall, mesmerizing blood red flower.  Its beautiful, pristine form is "
"rooted firmly on the innards of the beast.  The flesh around it is decayed, "
"being consumed to feed its ornate, magnanimous body.  You feel an urge to "
"sit and admire this priceless miracle of life."
msgstr ""
"血のように赤く魅惑的な花をつけた、非常に背の高い植物です。美しく清らかな姿ですが、モンスターの肉体にしっかりと根付いているようです。可憐かつ壮大な花を養うために周囲の肉の養分は吸い取られ、腐敗しています。このかけがえのない生命の奇跡をじっと眺めていたいという衝動に駆られます。"

#. ~ Bashing sound
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_nether_monster.json
msgid "a chilling scream!"
msgstr "[ぞっとする叫び声！]"

#. ~ Bashing failed sound
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_nether_monster.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/maps/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_floraxeno.json
msgid "squish!"
msgstr "グシャッ！"

#. ~ Player message in nested effect in effect in EoC "admire_lily_effect" in
#. examine action of furniture "beautiful nether lily"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_nether_monster.json
msgid "You admire the lily.  Isn't it beautiful?"
msgstr "異界のユリを賞賛しました。なんて美しいのでしょう？"

#. ~ Player message in nested effect in effect in EoC "admire_lily_effect" in
#. examine action of furniture "beautiful nether lily"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_nether_monster.json
msgid "You worship the lily, and feel truly fulfilled."
msgstr "異界のユリを褒め称え、心の底から充実感に満ちています。"

#. ~ Player message in nested effect in effect in EoC "admire_lily_effect" in
#. examine action of furniture "beautiful nether lily"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_nether_monster.json
msgid "You bow to the lily, and gain immense satisfaction in having done so."
msgstr "異界のユリにこうべを垂れ、計り知れない満足感を得ました。"

#. ~ Player message in nested effect in effect in EoC "admire_lily_effect" in
#. examine action of furniture "beautiful nether lily"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_nether_monster.json
msgid "You focus on the lily and realize it truly is perfection *incarnate*."
msgstr "異界のユリを眺め、本当に完璧な*姿*であることを認識しました。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_nether_monster.json
msgid "nether grass"
msgstr "異界の草地"

#. ~ Description of furniture "nether grass"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_nether_monster.json
msgid ""
"A bed of waist high segmented blue plants that remind you of grass.  As you "
"wade past, they react to your movement and always swivel to face you."
msgstr ""
"草でできたベッドを思わせる、腰の高さまで伸びた青色の植物です。草を掻き分けて通ろうとすると、全ての葉がその動きに反応し、身をよじって纏わりつこうとします。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_nether_monster.json
msgid "tall nether grass"
msgstr "生い茂った異界の草地"

#. ~ Description of furniture "tall nether grass"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_nether_monster.json
msgid ""
"A clump of tall, segmented blue plants that remind you of grass.  As you "
"approach, they bend towards you, hugging your body and making movement "
"difficult."
msgstr "一般的な草に似た、背が高く所々に節がある青色の植物が生い茂っています。近付くと葉がぴったりと身を寄せてきて、動きを阻害します。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_nether_monster.json
msgid "nether patchwork"
msgstr "絡み合った異界植物"

#. ~ Description of furniture "nether patchwork"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_nether_monster.json
msgid ""
"A peculiar plant that is hard to distinguish, resembling a tangled mess of "
"different terrestrial flowers and weeds firmly wedged into the monstrous "
"flesh.  It pulses rhythmically as it rearranges its form into even weirder "
"shapes."
msgstr ""
"様々な変わった草花がモンスターの肉体にしっかりと根付き、互いに絡み合って一塊になっています。リズミカルに脈打ちながら、更に奇妙な形状へと変化し続けています。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_nether_monster.json
msgid "nether lichen"
msgstr "異界の地衣類"

#. ~ Description of furniture "nether lichen"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_nether_monster.json
msgid ""
"A bed of orange, flowering lichen, covering the surface of the yellow ichor."
"  Every now and then, a flower disappears into the liquid, but seems to "
"reappear the moment you look away."
msgstr ""
"黄色い液体の表面を覆うように、オレンジ色の花を咲かせる地衣類が繁茂しています。花は時折落ちて液体の中へと消えていきますが、あっという間に再び開花します。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_refrigeration.json
#: data/mods/BlazeIndustries/vehicleparts/blaze_other_parts.json
msgid "refrigerator"
msgstr "冷蔵庫"

#. ~ Description of furniture "refrigerator"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_refrigeration.json
msgid ""
"A standard household refrigerator.  If powered, it will cool its contents to"
" extend the time before they spoil.  Deconstruct it if you want to connect "
"it to the grid."
msgstr ""
"一般的な家庭用冷蔵庫です。電源が入っていると内容物が冷やされ、腐るまでの期間が延長されます。電気配線に接続する場合は取り外す必要があります。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "minifridge"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_refrigeration.json
msgid ""
"A small fridge, often used in places where full-size fridge would be too big"
" or too much a hassle to transport, or when you only need a small amount of "
"items chilled.  Deconstruct it if you want to connect it to the grid."
msgstr ""
"小型の冷蔵庫です。一般的なサイズの冷蔵庫を置くには場所が狭すぎるか運搬が困難な場合、容量がそれほど必要ない場合などによく使われます。電気配線に接続する場合は取り外す必要があります。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "single glass door fridge"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_refrigeration.json
msgid ""
"A modern refrigerator with a thick sheet of glass for a door, used in stores"
" to show off the goods while keeping them cool.  Deconstruct it if you want "
"to connect it to the grid."
msgstr ""
"厚いガラスドアが付いている現代的な冷蔵庫です。冷やした商品を陳列するために店舗で使われます。電気配線に接続する場合は取り外す必要があります。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "double glass door fridge"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_refrigeration.json
msgid ""
"A modern refrigerator with two glass doors, to fit twice as much goods for "
"consumers.  Deconstruct it if you want to connect it to the grid."
msgstr "2枚の厚いガラスドアが付いている、2倍の量の商品を陳列できる現代的な冷蔵庫です。電気配線に接続する場合は取り外す必要があります。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "heavy-duty fridge"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_refrigeration.json
msgid ""
"A heavy, bulky refrigerator, used in professional kitchens.  Deconstruct it "
"if you want to connect it to the grid."
msgstr "店舗の厨房で使われる重厚な冷蔵庫です。電気配線に接続する場合は取り外す必要があります。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "display fridge"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_refrigeration.json
msgid ""
"A big glass chamber, designed to display different food in multiple rows, "
"while cooling it at the same time.  Looks gorgeous, but has nothing good to "
"show to you.  Deconstruct it if you want to connect it to the grid."
msgstr ""
"ガラスドアが付いた大型の冷蔵ショーケースです。様々な食品を冷やした状態で複数の列に並べることができます。見た目は豪華ですが、何を陳列すべきか分かりません。電気配線に接続する場合は取り外す必要があります。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "minifreezer"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_refrigeration.json
msgid ""
"A small upright freezer, used to store a small amount of perishables long "
"term.  Deconstruct it if you want to connect it to the grid."
msgstr "少量の生鮮食品を長期保存するために使う、縦長の小型冷凍庫です。電気配線に接続する場合は取り外す必要があります。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "chest minifreezer"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_refrigeration.json
msgid ""
"A small chest freezer, used to store a small amount of perishables for a "
"long time, if you're willing to dig them out each time that is.  Deconstruct"
" it if you want to connect it to the grid."
msgstr ""
"少量の生鮮食品を長期保存し、必要になったらその都度掘り返して取り出す、小型冷凍ストッカーです。電気配線に接続する場合は取り外す必要があります。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "chest freezer"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_refrigeration.json
msgid ""
"A chest freezer.  Big and power efficient, this is the dream for every "
"cataclysm survivor.  Deconstruct it if you want to connect it to the grid."
msgstr "冷凍ストッカーは容量が大きく電力効率もいい、大変動を生き延びた全ての者にとっての憧れです。電気配線に接続する場合は取り外す必要があります。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "heavy-duty freezer"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_refrigeration.json
msgid ""
"A heavy-duty upright freezer, one that is used in a professional kitchen.  "
"Deconstruct it if you want to connect it to the grid."
msgstr "店舗の厨房で使われる重厚な縦長の冷蔵庫です。電気配線に接続する場合は取り外す必要があります。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "glass door freezer"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_refrigeration.json
msgid ""
"A commercial upright freezer, used to show ice creams, frozen veggies, "
"pizza, or anything else a consumer may want frozen and preserved.  "
"Deconstruct it if you want to connect it to the grid."
msgstr ""
"縦長の業務用冷凍庫です。アイスクリーム、冷凍野菜、ピザなどの商品を冷凍した状態で陳列できます。電気配線に接続する場合は取り外す必要があります。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_refrigeration.json
msgid "display chest freezer"
msgstr "横型冷凍ショーケース"

#. ~ Description of furniture "display chest freezer"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_refrigeration.json
msgid ""
"A commercial chest freezer, used to show off ice creams, frozen veggies, "
"pizza, or anything else a consumer may want frozen and preserved.  "
"Conveniently tall enough for any curious child to gaze in at the sweets.  "
"Deconstruct it if you want to connect it to the grid."
msgstr ""
"横長の業務用冷凍庫です。アイスクリーム、冷凍野菜、ピザなどの商品を冷凍した状態で陳列できます。好奇心旺盛な子供がお菓子をじっくり眺められる程度の高さがあります。電気配線に接続する場合は取り外す必要があります。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
msgid "black glass figure"
msgstr "黒ガラスの像"

#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass figure"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
msgid ""
"A black glass figure of a someone frozen halfway through falling backwards, "
"and suspended on a single leg."
msgstr "後ろに倒れ込み、片足だけで体を支えている格好のまま固まっている、黒いガラスでできた像です。"

#. ~ Bashing failed sound
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
msgid "tink."
msgstr "カツン。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass figure"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
msgid "A black glass figure of a person covering their face with their hands."
msgstr "顔を手で覆うポーズをしている、黒いガラスでできた像です。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass figure"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
msgid ""
"A black glass figure of a child.  It is difficult to make out their facial "
"features, but it seems as if they are smiling."
msgstr "黒いガラスでできた、子供サイズの像です。顔の特徴は分かりにくいですが、笑っているようです。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass figure"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
msgid "A black glass figure of someone kneeling in prayer."
msgstr "跪いて祈るポーズをしている、黒いガラスでできた像です。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass figure"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
msgid ""
"A black glass figure of someone in a firing posture.  Their jagged fingers "
"are frozen squeezing a trigger that isn't there."
msgstr "発砲しているようなポーズの、黒いガラスでできた像です。尖った指は、そこにない引き金を握ろうとする形のまま固まっています。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass figure"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
msgid ""
"A black glass figure of someone leaning into the space to their right, their"
" fingers bent as if interlaced with someone else's."
msgstr "右側に身を乗り出し、指は何かを握るように曲げているポーズの、黒いガラスでできた像です。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass figure"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
msgid ""
"A black glass figure of someone clutching at their neck.  A delicate spray "
"of connected glass droplets emerges between their fingers."
msgstr "誰かに首を掴まれているような姿勢の、黒いガラスでできた像です。指の間で、繊細なガラスの筋がまるで液体のように拡散しています。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass figure"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
msgid ""
"Most of a black glass human figure.  The face and much of the head is "
"missing, as if scooped out, and the inner surface is perfectly smooth."
msgstr "黒いガラスでできた、人間のように見える像です。頭部の大部分は抉られたように欠落しており、表面は滑らかです。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass figure"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
msgid "A black glass figure of someone doubled over in laughter."
msgstr "身体をくの字に曲げて笑っている姿の、黒いガラスでできた像です。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass figure"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
msgid ""
"A black glass figure.  Their features are too jagged to make out clearly, "
"but they remind you of someone you knew."
msgstr "黒いガラスでできた像です。表面がギザギザしており細かい特徴は分かりませんが、知り合いに似ているような気がします。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass figure"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
msgid ""
"A black glass figure of someone in a fighting stance, their face twisted "
"with howls of rage and anger.  They're gripping some sort of weapon that "
"isn't there."
msgstr "怒りと激情に顔を歪ませて叫び戦闘態勢をとる、黒いガラスでできた像です。武器を構えているかのように虚空を握っています。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
msgid "black glass bed"
msgstr "黒ガラスのベッド"

#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass bed"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
msgid ""
"A black glass sculpture of a bed.  The rumpled covers are jagged, and "
"splinter at the touch."
msgstr "黒いガラスでできたベッドです。皺だらけのカバーもギザギザのガラスで作られており、触ると割れてしまいます。"

#. ~ Bashing failed sound
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
msgid "clink."
msgstr "パキン。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
msgid "black glass bathtub"
msgstr "黒ガラスの浴槽"

#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass bathtub"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
msgid ""
"A tub made from black glass, with a frozen column of onyx pouring from the "
"tap."
msgstr "黒いガラスでできた浴槽です。蛇口からは、凍った水のようにオニキス色の柱が流れ出しています。"

#. ~ Bashing sound
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/furniture.json
msgid "glass shattering!"
msgstr "[ガラスが粉々に砕ける音！]"

#. ~ Bashing failed sound
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
msgid "clink!"
msgstr "カキン！"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
msgid "black glass dresser"
msgstr "黒ガラスの衣装棚"

#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass dresser"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
msgid ""
"A black glass cabinet with its doors slightly ajar.  Inside is a row of "
"hangers bearing neatly folded and entirely rigid clothing."
msgstr "扉が少し開いた状態の、黒いガラスでできた衣装棚です。内部では、完全に硬化した衣装がハンガーにかかって整然と並んでいます。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
msgid "black glass refrigerator"
msgstr "黒ガラスの冷蔵庫"

#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass refrigerator"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
msgid ""
"A black glass refrigerator, its door hanging open.  Inside is a seamless "
"surface with protrusions resembling fresh fruit and plastic bottles."
msgstr "扉が開け放たれたままの、黒いガラスでできた冷蔵庫です。内部の表面は滑らかで、新鮮な果物やペットボトルのように見える膨らみが並んでいます。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
msgid "black glass armchair"
msgstr "黒ガラスの肘掛け椅子"

#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass armchair"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
msgid ""
"An armchair that was presumably once very plush and comfortable.  Now the "
"overstuffed cushions are hard, cold, and slippery."
msgstr "普通の素材であれば非常に豪華で快適だったであろう肘掛け椅子です。これはクッションが硬く、冷たく、滑らかすぎます。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
msgid "black glass chair"
msgstr "黒ガラスの肘掛け椅子"

#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass chair"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
msgid ""
"A simple glass chair.  The seat is very thin, and crunches ominously under "
"any weight."
msgstr "シンプルなガラス製の椅子です。座面は非常に薄く、少しでも体重をかけると、ミシミシと嫌な音を発します。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
msgid "black glass desk"
msgstr "黒ガラスのデスク"

#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass desk"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
msgid ""
"A glass desk.  There are a handful of shapes atop it that suggest pens, "
"paper, and miscellaneous knickknacks that are too jagged to identify."
msgstr "ガラスでできた机です。机上にはペンや紙、小物類と思しき形状の膨らみがありますが、ギザギザしており識別し辛い状態です。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
msgid "black glass locker"
msgstr "黒ガラスのロッカー"

#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass locker"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
msgid ""
"A tall glass cabinet.  Whatever was inside will stay that way; the door is "
"seamless with the frame."
msgstr "ガラスでできた背の高い衣装棚です。中にあった荷物もそのまま残っていますが、扉と骨組みは癒着して一体になっています。"

#. ~ Bashing sound
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-windows.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
msgid "glass crunching!"
msgstr "[ガラスが細かく砕ける音！]"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
msgid "black glass oven"
msgstr "黒ガラスのオーブン"

#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass oven"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
msgid ""
"A glass sculpture of a gas oven.  Bristling from the burner is a crown of "
"jagged shards in the rough shape of an uncontrolled fire."
msgstr "ガラスでできたガスオーブンです。バーナーの部分からは、荒々しい炎を象ったギザギザの冠が立ち上っています。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
msgid "black glass mailbox"
msgstr "黒ガラスの郵便受け"

#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass mailbox"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
msgid ""
"A glass sculpture of a mailbox.  The door is open; inside is a pile of "
"envelopes, all razor-edged."
msgstr "ガラスでできた郵便受けです。扉は開いており、中に溜まった封筒の山はカミソリ刃のように尖っています。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
msgid "black glass display rack"
msgstr "黒ガラスの陳列棚"

#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass display rack"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
msgid ""
"A glass sculpture of a shelving unit.  The angled shelves are covered in "
"jagged miscellany, most of which is firmly fused in place."
msgstr "ガラスでできた棚です。歪んだ棚板の上には雑多な物が並んでいますが、そのほとんどは置かれた位置にしっかりと接着されています。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
msgid "black glass sink"
msgstr "黒ガラスの流し台"

#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass sink"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
msgid ""
"A glass basin and tap.  The inside stops halfway down in sheet of concentric"
" ripples, with the tiny spire of a splashing droplet at the center "
msgstr "ガラスでできた洗面台と蛇口です。洗面台の表面には同心円状の波紋ができており、中央には飛び散る水滴を象ったガラスの尖塔がそびえています。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
msgid "black glass toilet"
msgstr "黒ガラスの便器"

#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass toilet"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
msgid ""
"A toilet made of black glass.  The lid, perhaps mercifully, is fused shut."
msgstr "黒いガラスでできたトイレです。幸いなことに、蓋は完全に閉じています。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
msgid "black glass cupboard"
msgstr "黒ガラスの戸棚"

#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass cupboard"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
msgid ""
"A black glass cupboard.  The doors are fused shut, but it presumably "
"contains glasses."
msgstr "黒いガラスでできた戸棚です。扉は閉まった状態で癒着していますが、恐らく中にもガラスが入っています。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
msgid "black glass garden"
msgstr "黒ガラスのプランター"

#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass garden"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
msgid ""
"A planter of dark glass.  Sharp, twisting glass sprouts emerge from the "
"black soil within."
msgstr "黒っぽいガラスでできたプランターです。内部の黒い土から、捻じれて尖ったガラスの芽が顔を出しています。"

#. ~ Bashing failed sound
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
msgid "plink!"
msgstr "ビィン！"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
msgid "black glass flower"
msgstr "黒ガラスの花"

#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass flower"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
msgid ""
"A delicate little thing; a wispy stem slightly bowed under the weight of "
"translucent petals.  The tiny barbs that line it are almost impossible to "
"see, until it crumbles in your fingers."
msgstr ""
"繊細で小さな植物です。細い茎は半透明の花弁の重みによってわずかにたわんでいます。小さな棘が並んでいますが、その存在に気付く前に手の中で粉々になってしまいます。"

#. ~ Bashing sound
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
msgid "tinkle."
msgstr "パリン。"

#. ~ Bashing failed sound
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
msgid "plink."
msgstr "パシッ。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
msgid "black glass bench"
msgstr "黒ガラスのベンチ"

#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass bench"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
msgid ""
"A long, low slab of black glass.  You can't tell if the fissures here and "
"there on the surface are natural cracks, or carved names."
msgstr "黒いガラスでできた、背が低く長いベンチです。表面のあちこちに亀裂がありますが、自然にできたのか、誰かが彫った痕なのか分かりません。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
msgid "black glass washer"
msgstr "黒ガラスの洗濯機"

#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass washer"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
msgid ""
"A glass washing machine.  The inside is completely filled with black sand, "
"some of which has spilled onto the floor."
msgstr "ガラスでできた洗濯機です。内部は黒い砂で満たされており、一部は漏れて床に零れ落ちています。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
msgid "black glass dryer"
msgstr "黒ガラスの乾燥機"

#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass dryer"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
msgid ""
"A mechanical dryer of black glass.  The door hangs open, and inside, you can"
" see a jumble of what might once have been clothes, now smashed to pieces."
msgstr "黒いガラスでできた電動乾燥機です。蓋は開いたままになっており、中にはかつて衣服だったであろう物体が粉々に砕けて散乱しています。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
msgid "black glass bookcase"
msgstr "黒ガラスの本棚"

#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass bookcase"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
msgid ""
"A heavy bookshelf, laden with books fused into the shelves and each other.  "
"You can make out titles on the spines, but the alphabet they're written in "
"is unfamiliar."
msgstr "重厚な本棚には本が詰め込まれており、棚と本との境界は癒着しています。背表紙に何かタイトルが書いてあるようですが、文字までは読み取れません。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
msgid "black glass counter"
msgstr "黒ガラスのカウンター"

#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass counter"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
msgid ""
"A thick cube of black glass.  On the surface, fused in place, are statues of"
" utensils and miscellany."
msgstr "黒いガラスでできた分厚い立方体です。表面には道具や雑貨と思しき膨らみが溶けて固定されています。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
msgid "black glass table"
msgstr "黒ガラスのテーブル"

#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass table"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
msgid ""
"A slab of smooth black glass on four stout legs.  In a few places, there is "
"shallowly rounded mass, like liquid spilled on the surface."
msgstr "4本の頑丈な脚の上に、滑らかな黒いガラス板が乗っています。表面に数か所、何か液体をこぼしたような薄く丸い痕が残っています。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
msgid "black glass birdbath"
msgstr "黒ガラスのバードバス"

#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass birdbath"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
msgid ""
"A glass pedestal and bowl.  Inside, frozen in the midst of washing itself in"
" the black sand, is the delicate figure of a bird."
msgstr "ガラスでできた台座の上にボウルが乗っています。ボウルの中では小さなガラスの鳥が、黒い砂で体を洗う姿勢のまま固まっています。"

#. ~ Bashing failed sound
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
msgid "clunk."
msgstr "カチ。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
msgid "black glass shower"
msgstr "黒ガラスのシャワー"

#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass shower"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
msgid ""
"From the head of this shower descend a dozen streams of thin black glass, "
"with frozen droplets strung from them like pearls."
msgstr "シャワーヘッドからは黒い半透明のガラスの筋が数十本垂れ下がっており、その下には凍り付き固まった水滴が真珠のように連なっています。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
msgid "black glass water heater"
msgstr "黒ガラスの給湯器"

#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass water heater"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
msgid ""
"A cylinder of thick black glass.  The top has burst apart, and rivulets of "
"black sand run down the side."
msgstr "黒いガラスでできた分厚い円筒容器です。上部が割れて、側面から黒い砂が小川のように流れ落ちています。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
msgid "black glass fireplace"
msgstr "黒ガラスの暖炉"

#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass fireplace"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
msgid ""
"A fireplace of pitted glass bricks.  The fire inside has been frozen in "
"glass at the moment it began to leap beyond the grate."
msgstr "ガラスでできた、内部が空洞になっている暖炉です。燃えていた火が火格子を飛び出そうとした瞬間に、凍り付いてガラスになってしまったようです。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
msgid "ring of black stones"
msgstr "黒い石組"

#. ~ Description of furniture "ring of black stones"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
msgid ""
"A circle of smooth glass pebbles.  Inside are frozen tendrils of fire, "
"slightly translucent.  It seems colder as you approach."
msgstr ""
"滑らかなガラスのような小石が環状に並んでいます。内側では、凍り付いた火のような半透明のオブジェが蔦のように立ち昇っています。近寄ると寒さを感じるような気がします。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
msgid "black glass lantern"
msgstr "黒ガラスの照明"

#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass lantern"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
msgid ""
"A tall glass pole with a translucent shade atop it.  You know it could not "
"possibly turn on, but in the corner of your eye, you think you might see a "
"soft glow."
msgstr "上部に半透明のランプシェードが付いた、ガラスでできた背の高いポールです。点灯する筈もありませんが、柔らかな光を放っているような気がします。"

#. ~ Bashing failed sound
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
msgid "tink!"
msgstr "カチン！"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
msgid "black glass box"
msgstr "黒ガラスの箱"

#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass box"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
msgid "A box of thin black glass.  Its edges are glisteningly sharp."
msgstr "薄く黒いガラスでできた箱です。角が鋭く尖っています。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
msgid "black glass sofa"
msgstr "黒ガラスのソファ"

#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass sofa"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
msgid "A long bench, padded with cold glass cushions."
msgstr "冷たいガラスのクッションが詰まった、横に長い椅子です。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
msgid "black glass dishwasher"
msgstr "黒ガラスの食器洗浄機"

#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass dishwasher"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
msgid ""
"A glass dishwasher, its door hanging open.  Inside, glass plates and "
"utensils are half buried in black sand."
msgstr "ガラスでできた、蓋が開いたままの食器洗浄機です。内部では、ガラスの皿や器が黒い砂に埋もれています。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
msgid "incomplete plush doll"
msgstr "不完全なぬいぐるみ"

#. ~ Description of furniture "incomplete plush doll"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
msgid "A soft plush torso, empty of features, is lying on this sofa."
msgstr "柔らかいぬいぐるみの胴体だけがソファに横たわっています。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass bookcase"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
msgid "This bookcase is missing a book."
msgstr "この本棚は1冊だけ本が足りません。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
msgid "walkway"
msgstr "通路"

#. ~ Description of terrain "walkway"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
msgid ""
"A metallic bridge commonly used in industrial settings to meet specified "
"safety standards."
msgstr "工業規格で決められた安全基準を満たす、一般的な金属製の橋です。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#. ~ Overmap terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
#: data/json/overmap/overmap_terrain/overmap_terrain_recreational.json
msgid "dock"
msgstr "桟橋"

#. ~ Description of terrain "dock"
#. ~ Description of terrain "shallow bridge"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
msgid "A wooden platform held by a support made of logs dug into the ground."
msgstr "地面に埋まった丸太によって支えられている、木製の足場です。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
msgid "deep dock pile"
msgstr "橋脚"

#. ~ Description of terrain "deep dock pile"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
msgid ""
"A sturdy pile made of wood extending all the way to the riverbed.  A frame "
"will be required to support a surface."
msgstr "水底まで伸びた木製の頑丈な杭です。橋板を支えるには橋桁が必要です。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
msgid "deep dock frame"
msgstr "橋桁"

#. ~ Description of terrain "deep dock frame"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
msgid ""
"A log frame secured atop a wooden pile.  Adding a wood surface will make "
"this into a proper dock section."
msgstr "木製の杭に固定された丸太の骨組みです。木製の橋板を固定すれば立派な桟橋になります。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
msgid "deep dock"
msgstr "桟橋(深水域)"

#. ~ Description of terrain "deep dock"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
msgid ""
"A wooden platform held by a tall wooden pile that extend to the riverbed.  "
"Very sturdy, and likely to outlast you."
msgstr "水底まで伸びた木製の頑丈な杭に支えられた、木製の桟橋です。非常に丈夫で長持ちしそうです。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
msgid "shallow bridge"
msgstr "桟橋"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
msgid "pontoon bridge"
msgstr "舟橋"

#. ~ Description of terrain "pontoon bridge"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
msgid ""
"A floating temporary bridge over still water, like the ones armies used to "
"make to cross lakes."
msgstr "軍隊が湖を渡るために設置するものに似た、流れのない水場に浮かぶ間に合わせの橋です。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
msgid "river bridge"
msgstr "河川橋"

#. ~ Description of terrain "river bridge"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
msgid ""
"A floating temporary bridge over flowing water, like the ones armies used to"
" make to cross rivers."
msgstr "軍隊が川を渡るために設置するものに似た、流水に浮かぶ間に合わせの橋です。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-highways.json
msgid "bridge pavement"
msgstr "道路(橋)"

#. ~ Description of terrain "bridge pavement"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-highways.json
msgid "A bridge section made out of concrete and metal."
msgstr "コンクリートと金属で作られた橋です。"

#. ~ Bashing sound
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-highways.json
msgid "concrete cracking and metal screeching!"
msgstr "[コンクリートや金属の破砕音]"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-highways.json
msgid "bridge yellow pavement"
msgstr "車線(橋)"

#. ~ Description of terrain "bridge yellow pavement"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-highways.json
msgid "A bridge section made out of concrete and metal.  It's painted yellow."
msgstr "コンクリートと金属で作られた橋です。黄色に塗られています。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-highways.json
msgid "bridge sidewalk"
msgstr "歩道(橋)"

#. ~ Description of terrain "bridge sidewalk"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-highways.json
msgid "The sidewalk section of a concrete bridge."
msgstr "コンクリート製の橋の歩道です。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "dock"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
msgid ""
"A metal platform held by a support made of concrete set into the ground."
msgstr "地面に埋まったコンクリート柱によって支えられている、金属製の足場です。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "deep dock pile"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
msgid ""
"A sturdy pile made of poured concrete extending all the way to the riverbed."
"  A metal frame will be required to support a surface."
msgstr "水底まで伸びたコンクリート製の頑丈な杭です。橋板を支えるには金属製の橋桁が必要です。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "deep dock frame"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
msgid ""
"A metal frame secured atop a concrete pile.  Adding a metal surface will "
"make this into a proper dock section."
msgstr "コンクリートの杭に固定された金属製の骨組みです。金属製の橋板を固定すれば立派な桟橋になります。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "deep dock"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
msgid ""
"A metal platform held by a tall metal pile that extends to the riverbed.  "
"Very sturdy, and likely to outlast you."
msgstr "水底まで伸びた頑丈な金属柱に支えられた、金属製の桟橋です。非常に丈夫で長持ちしそうです。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
msgid "metal floating dock"
msgstr "浮き船渠"

#. ~ Description of terrain "metal floating dock"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
msgid "A floating temporary dock, anchored to keep it from drifting away."
msgstr "漂流しないように固定された、一時的な浮き船渠です。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "closed laminated glass door"
msgstr "閉じたドア(合わせガラス)"

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed laminated glass door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A closed laminated glass door, composed of layers of glass and plastic held "
"together by an interlayer."
msgstr "ガラス層とプラスチック層を中間膜で結合した、透明な閉じたドアです。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "open laminated glass door"
msgstr "開いたドア(合わせガラス)"

#. ~ Description of terrain "open laminated glass door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A laminated glass door, composed of layers of glass and plastic held "
"together by an interlayer.  It's open."
msgstr "ガラス層とプラスチック層を中間膜で結合した透明なドアです。開け放たれています。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "closed ballistic glass door"
msgstr "閉じたドア(防弾ガラス)"

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed ballistic glass door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "A ballistic glass door, consisting of layers of laminated glass."
msgstr "合わせガラスを層状に重ねた防弾ガラス製のドアです。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "open ballistic glass door"
msgstr "開いたドア(防弾ガラス)"

#. ~ Description of terrain "open ballistic glass door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A ballistic glass door, consisting of layers of laminated glass.  It's open."
msgstr "合わせガラスを層状に重ねた防弾ガラス製のドアです。開け放たれています。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "closed reinforced glass door"
msgstr "閉じたドア(強化ガラス)"

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed reinforced glass door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A closed glass door reinforced with woven steel wires in a stylish, but "
"practical pattern."
msgstr "鋼鉄ワイヤーで補強された、スタイリッシュかつ実用的なガラス製の閉じた扉です。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "open reinforced glass door"
msgstr "開いたドア(強化ガラス)"

#. ~ Description of terrain "open reinforced glass door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A glass door reinforced with woven steel wires in a stylish, but practical "
"pattern.  It's open."
msgstr "鋼鉄ワイヤーで補強された、スタイリッシュかつ実用的なガラス製の扉です。開け放たれています。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "closed wood door"
msgstr "閉じたドア(木)"

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed wood door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A standard wooden door that doesn't look very resilient.  It'd probably burn"
" easily, too."
msgstr "標準的な木製の扉です。あまり頑丈な作りには見えず、簡単に燃えそうです。"

#. ~ Prying message of terrain "closed wood door"
#. ~ Prying message of terrain "closed wood door with peephole"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "You notice the door is unlocked, so you simply open it."
msgstr "施錠されていないことに気づいたので、そのままドアを開けました。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "closed wood door with an electronic lock"
msgstr "電子ロック付きの閉じたドア(木)"

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed wood door with an electronic lock"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A standard wooden door that doesn't look very resilient.  It'd probably burn"
" easily, too.  This one has a deadbolt electronic lock, so it's likely "
"locked.  You could pry it open, guessing the code is out of the question, or"
" unlock the deadbolt from the inside."
msgstr ""
"標準的な木製の扉です。あまり頑丈な作りには見えず、簡単に燃えそうです。電子ロック式の差し錠が付いており、ロックされているようですが、こじ開ける道具を使うか、暗証番号を入力するか、内側に回って解錠すれば開けられそうです。"

#. ~ Prying message of terrain "closed wood door with an electronic lock"
#. ~ Prying message of terrain "closed wood door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "You pry open the door."
msgstr "ドアをこじ開けました。"

#. ~ Prying failure of terrain "closed wood door with an electronic lock"
#. ~ Prying failure of terrain "closed wood door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "You pry, but can't pry open the door."
msgstr "ドアをこじ開けようとしましたが、失敗しました。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed wood door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A regular door made of ordinary wood, except this one has a peephole.  If "
"you examined it more closely, you'd be able to peek through the hole.  This "
"one has a deadbolt numpad, so it's likely locked.  You could pry it open, "
"guessing the code is out of the question, or unlock the deadbolt from the "
"inside."
msgstr ""
"覗き穴が開いている、一般的な木製の扉です。近寄って調べると穴から向こう側を覗けます。スライド鍵が付いており、ロックされているようですが、こじ開ける道具を使うか、内側に回って解錠すれば開けられそうです。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed wood door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A standard wooden door that doesn't look very resilient.  It'd probably burn"
" easily, too.  This one has an electronic keypad, so it's likely locked.  "
"You could pry it open, guessing the code is out of the question."
msgstr ""
"標準的な木製の扉です。あまり頑丈な作りには見えず、簡単に燃えそうです。キーパッドが付いており、電子錠でロックされているようですが、こじ開ける道具を使えば開けられそうですが、暗証番号を推測するなんてできそうにありません。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "open wood door"
msgstr "開いたドア(木)"

#. ~ Description of terrain "open wood door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A standard wooden door that doesn't look very resilient.  It'd probably burn"
" easily, too.  This one is wide open."
msgstr "標準的な木製の扉です。あまり頑丈な作りには見えず、簡単に燃えそうです。大きく開け放たれています。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "damaged wood door"
msgstr "損傷したドア(木)"

#. ~ Description of terrain "damaged wood door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A trashed wooden door, with a large hole in the middle that you can see "
"right through.  The doorknob is so messed up that it can't be opened "
"anymore.  It could be fixed up with a few planks."
msgstr ""
"役に立たない木製のドアです。中央に大きな穴が開いており、向こう側が見渡せます。ドアノブも折れ曲がり壊れています。木材を何枚か使えば修理できるかもしれません。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "empty door frame"
msgstr "ドア枠"

#. ~ Description of terrain "empty door frame"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"An empty door frame made from planks and nails.  A variety of doors could be"
" constructed here."
msgstr "木材と釘で作られたドア枠です。ここに様々な扉を建設できます。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "closed glass door"
msgstr "閉じたドア(ガラス)"

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed glass door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A sliding glass door, clear enough that an animal or a particularly dumb "
"person could slam right into it.  This one is closed, so don't hurt "
"yourself."
msgstr ""
"動物や大間抜けな人間がぶつかってもおかしくないくらい透明な、ガラス製の引き戸です。現在ドアは閉まっているので、ぶつからないよう気を付けましょう。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "open glass door"
msgstr "開いたドア(ガラス)"

#. ~ Description of terrain "open glass door"
#. ~ Description of terrain "open frosted glass door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A sliding glass door that has been left open for all manner of things to "
"travel through."
msgstr "ガラス製のスライドドアです。開き切っており、あらゆるものの通行を妨げません。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "closed lighthouse lens hinged section"
msgstr "閉じた灯台レンズ"

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed lighthouse lens hinged section"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"An intricate arrangement of glass, designed to focus light from within to be"
" visible over long distances.  This section of the lens is on hinges and can"
" be opened for maintenance."
msgstr ""
"内部の光を集めて遠くまで届けるための、複雑な形状に組み合わされたガラス製レンズです。この側面は蝶番で固定されており、メンテナンスの際に開けられる作りになっています。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "open lighthouse lens hinged section"
msgstr "開いた灯台レンズ"

#. ~ Description of terrain "open lighthouse lens hinged section"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"An intricate arrangement of glass, designed to focus light from within to be"
" visible over long distances.  This section of the lens is hinged and is "
"currently open."
msgstr "内部の光を集めて遠くまで届けるために、ガラスが複雑な形状に組み合わさっています。この側面は蝶番で固定されており、現在は開いています。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "closed wood door with peephole"
msgstr "ドアスコープ付きの閉じたドア(木)"

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed wood door with peephole"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A regular door made of ordinary wood, except this one has a peephole.  If "
"you examined it more closely, you'd be able to peek through the hole."
msgstr "覗き穴が開いている、一般的な木製の扉です。近寄って調べると穴から向こう側を覗けます。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "damaged wood door with peephole"
msgstr "ドアスコープ付きの損傷したドア(木)"

#. ~ Description of terrain "damaged wood door with peephole"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"The bad news is that the peephole is broken and you can't use it to look "
"through the door.  The good news is that the door is nearly broken down, so "
"there's nothing blocking the view.  Also, the doorknob is so messed up that "
"it can't be opened anymore.  A few planks, nails, and the right tools could "
"patch up all the damage."
msgstr ""
"悪い知らせは、覗き穴が壊れていて向こう側を覗けないことです。良い知らせは、ドアに大穴が開いているので向こう側がばっちり見渡せることです。木材や釘、そして適切な工具があれば損傷を修復できます。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "open wood door with peephole"
msgstr "ドアスコープ付きの開いたドア(木)"

#. ~ Description of terrain "open wood door with peephole"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A regular door made of ordinary wood, except this one has a peephole.  If "
"you examined it more closely, you'd be able to peek through the hole.  No "
"need right now though, since the door is open anyway."
msgstr ""
"覗き穴が開いている、一般的な木製の扉です。近寄って調べると穴から向こう側を覗けます。ドアが開いた状態なので、わざわざ覗き見る必要はありませんね。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "closed reinforced wood door"
msgstr "閉じた補強ドア(木)"

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed reinforced wood door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"Just like other wooden doors, except this one has layers of nailed-on planks"
" and an additional hinge for reinforcement.  It might be barricaded, but "
"it's still susceptible to fire."
msgstr "一般的な木製の扉ですが、木材が釘で固定され、補強のために蝶番が追加されています。頑丈さは増したものの、燃えやすさは元のままです。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "damaged reinforced wood door"
msgstr "損傷した補強ドア(木)"

#. ~ Description of terrain "damaged reinforced wood door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"Despite someone's best efforts at reinforcing this door, there are "
"splintering planks and visible holes in the wood, it could soon be smashed "
"apart completely if not repaired.  The doorknob is all messed up and the "
"door can't be opened until it's fixed."
msgstr ""
"懸命な補強が施されたにもかかわらず、板が割れ、穴が開いてしまったドアです。そのまま放っておけば、いずれ完全に壊されてしまいそうです。ドアノブも折れ曲がっており、直すまで開けません。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "open reinforced wood door"
msgstr "開いた補強ドア(木)"

#. ~ Description of terrain "open reinforced wood door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"Just like other wooden doors, except this one has layers of nailed-on planks"
" for reinforcement.  It might be fortified, but it's still susceptible to "
"fire.  It's open, so it's not stopping anything right now."
msgstr ""
"一般的な木製の扉ですが、複数の木材を釘で打ち付けて補強してあります。頑丈さは増したものの、燃えやすさは元のままです。大きく開いている今の状態では何の障壁にもなりません。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed wood door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A standard wooden door that doesn't look very resilient.  It'd probably burn"
" easily, too.  This one has an extra keyhole, so it's likely locked.  You "
"could pry it open or pick the lock."
msgstr ""
"標準的な木製の扉です。あまり頑丈な作りには見えず、簡単に燃えそうです。鍵穴が付いており、ロックされている可能性がありますが、こじ開ける道具やロックピックを使えば開けられそうです。"

#. ~ Lockpick message of terrain "closed wood door"
#. ~ Lockpick message of terrain "t_door_metal_interior_locked"
#. ~ Lockpick message of terrain "closed metal door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "With a satisfying click, the lock on the door opens."
msgstr "カチッと音がして、ドアの鍵が開きました。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed wood door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A standard wooden door that doesn't look very resilient.  It'd probably burn"
" easily, too.  This one has a deadbolt keyhole, so it's likely locked.  You "
"could pry it open or pick the lock, or unlock the deadbolt from the inside."
msgstr ""
"標準的な木製の扉です。あまり頑丈な作りには見えず、簡単に燃えそうです。スライド鍵が付いており、ロックされている可能性がありますが、こじ開ける道具やロックピックを使うか、内側に回って解錠すれば開けられそうです。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed wood door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A regular door made of ordinary wood, except this one has a peephole.  If "
"you examined it more closely, you'd be able to peek through the hole.  This "
"one has a deadbolt keyhole, so it's likely locked.  You could pry it open or"
" pick the lock, or unlock the deadbolt from the inside."
msgstr ""
"覗き穴が開いている、一般的な木製の扉です。近寄って調べると穴から向こう側を覗けます。スライド鍵が付いており、ロックされている可能性がありますが、こじ開ける道具やロックピックを使うか、内側に回って解錠すれば開けられそうです。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "closed door curtain"
msgstr "閉じたドアカーテン"

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed door curtain"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"Repurposed curtains from a window covering a door frame.  Could be easily "
"taken down for supplies or placed somewhere else."
msgstr "窓用のカーテンを再利用して戸口を覆いました。取り外しが簡単なため、外して素材を活用したり他の場所に付け替えたりできます。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "closed makeshift door"
msgstr "閉じた簡易ドア"

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed makeshift door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A makeshift screen consisting of planks bound together with rope, hanging "
"vertically from the top of the doorway.  Could be easily taken down and re-"
"purposed."
msgstr "紐で木材を束ねてドア枠の上部から吊るした簡単な仕切りです。すぐに取り外して再利用できます。"

#. ~ Bashing failed sound
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "wham."
msgstr "ドカン。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "open door curtain"
msgstr "開いたドアカーテン"

#. ~ Description of terrain "open door curtain"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"Repurposed curtains from a window covering a door frame.  Could be easily "
"taken down for supplies or placed somewhere else.  The curtains are open, "
"bundled, and tied next to the doorway."
msgstr ""
"窓用のカーテンを再利用して戸口を覆いました。取り外しが簡単なため、外して素材を活用したり他の場所に付け替えたりできます。カーテンは戸口の脇に束ねられています。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "closed grass curtain"
msgstr "閉じた草編みドアカーテン"

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed grass curtain"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"Sheets of grass yarn covering a door frame.  Could be easily taken down for "
"supplies or placed somewhere else."
msgstr "植物を編んで作ったカーテンで戸口を覆いました。取り外しが簡単なため、外して素材を活用したり他の場所に付け替えたりできます。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "open grass curtain"
msgstr "開いた草編みドアカーテン"

#. ~ Description of terrain "open grass curtain"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"Sheets of grass yarn covering a door frame.  Could be easily taken down for "
"supplies or placed somewhere else.  The curtains are open, bundled, and tied"
" next to the doorway."
msgstr ""
"植物を編んで作ったカーテンで戸口を覆いました。取り外しが簡単なため、外して素材を活用したり他の場所に付け替えたりできます。カーテンは戸口の脇に束ねられています。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "open makeshift door"
msgstr "開いた簡易ドア"

#. ~ Description of terrain "open makeshift door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A makeshift screen consisting of planks bound together with rope, hanging "
"from the top of the doorway.  Could be easily taken down and re-purposed.  "
"The planks have been rolled up and attached to the top of the doorway, "
"allowing free movement through."
msgstr ""
"紐で木材を束ねてドア枠の上部から吊るした簡単な仕切りです。すぐに取り外して再利用できます。木材は戸口の上部に巻き取られており、自由に出入りできます。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "empty metal door frame"
msgstr "ドア枠(金属)"

#. ~ Description of terrain "empty metal door frame"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"An empty door frame made of steel and assorted metal.  A variety of doors "
"could be constructed here."
msgstr "鉄などの金属類で作られたドア枠です。ここに様々な扉を建設できます。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "empty metal window frame"
msgstr "窓枠(金属)"

#. ~ Description of terrain "empty metal window frame"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"An empty window frame constructed from assembled metal and carefully braced "
"with various hardware."
msgstr "金属を組み合わせて丁寧に補強した窓枠です。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "boarded up door"
msgstr "板張りされたドア"

#. ~ Description of terrain "boarded up door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A standard wooden door that has several planks across it, nailed down to "
"board it up and increase its durability.  It's still flammable, though."
msgstr "一般的な木製の扉ですが、複数の木材を釘で打ち付けて補強してあります。頑丈さは増したものの、燃えやすさは元のままです。"

#. ~ Prying message of terrain "boarded up door"
#. ~ Prying message of terrain "boarded up damaged door"
#. ~ Prying message of terrain "boarded up door with peephole"
#. ~ Prying message of terrain "boarded up reinforced door"
#. ~ Prying message of terrain "boarded up damaged reinforced door"
#. ~ Prying message of terrain "boarded up damaged door with peephole"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "You pry the boards from the door."
msgstr "ドアから板を取り外しました。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "boarded up damaged door"
msgstr "損傷した板張りドア"

#. ~ Description of terrain "boarded up damaged door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A boarded up wooden door, except that some of the planks are fractured or "
"coming loose.  Without repairs, it could be broken down easily."
msgstr "木製の扉に板が張り付けられていますが、何枚かは破損が見られ、打ち付けが緩んでいます。修理しなければ簡単に壊れてしまいます。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "boarded up door with peephole"
msgstr "ドアスコープ付きの損傷した板張りドア"

#. ~ Description of terrain "boarded up door with peephole"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A boarded up door made of ordinary wood, except this one has a peephole.  "
"Although it's been covered up in planks, you could still look through the "
"peephole if you were close enough."
msgstr "覗き穴がある木製の扉です。木材で隙間なく覆われ補強されていますが、覗き穴は塞がっておらず、近寄れば向こう側を覗き見ることができます。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "boarded up reinforced door"
msgstr "板張り補強ドア"

#. ~ Description of terrain "boarded up reinforced door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"An additionally reinforced door of layered planks that has been boarded up "
"with more wood to prevent it from opening.  It's still susceptible to fire."
msgstr "開かないようにより多くの木材で補強した、頑丈な扉です。燃えやすさは以前と変わりません。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "boarded up damaged reinforced door"
msgstr "損傷した板張り補強ドア"

#. ~ Description of terrain "boarded up damaged reinforced door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A battered and torn reinforced door with planks bursting from the joints.  "
"The boarded up planks are fragmented and in pieces, this doesn't look like "
"an easy repair."
msgstr "補強された扉の所々に穴が開いています。補強に使われていた木材も壊れてしまっており、容易に修復できそうにありません。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "boarded up damaged door with peephole"
msgstr "ドアスコープ付きの損傷した板張り補強ドア"

#. ~ Description of terrain "boarded up damaged door with peephole"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A wrecked door made of ordinary wood, except this one has a peephole and "
"some partly-splintered boards nailed across it.  The peephole is damaged and"
" can't be used to see through."
msgstr "一部に木材が釘で打ち付けられている、覗き穴が開いた一般的な木製の扉です。覗き穴が破損しており、向こう側が見えません。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/maps/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_habitat_doors.json
msgid "closed metal door"
msgstr "閉じたドア(金属)"

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed metal door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"An extremely resilient door made of assorted steel, carved and pounded into "
"shape."
msgstr "削り出しと鍛造によって成形された合金鋼製の非常に強靭な扉です。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "closed corrugated metal door"
msgstr "閉じたドア(トタン板)"

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed corrugated metal door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "A thin door made of corrugated steel held in a frame."
msgstr "波状の鉄板を枠に嵌めて作った薄いドアです。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "metal wall"
msgstr "壁(金属)"

#. ~ Description of terrain "metal wall"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid ""
"An industrially fabricated thick sheet carefully positioned and joined "
"seamlessly with perimeter sealant, this wall is capable of resisting extreme"
" elements as well as hostile forces.  Blast load rated and extremely fire-"
"retardant, breaching it will require specialized tools or an industrial "
"vehicle."
msgstr ""
"縁に密閉剤を丁寧に塗り込んだ工業規格の分厚い鉄板が、規則正しく並んでいます。この壁は厳しい環境に加えて強い衝撃にも耐性があります。爆風に強く、難燃性も高いため、突破するには特殊な工具か重機が必要です。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "open secret door"
msgstr "開いた隠し扉"

#. ~ Description of terrain "open secret door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"This apparently normal segment of metal wall has opened to reveal a secret "
"passage."
msgstr "何の変哲もない金属製の壁が開き、秘密の通路が現れました。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "concrete wall"
msgstr "壁(ｺﾝｸﾘｰﾄ)"

#. ~ Description of terrain "concrete wall"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A faux concrete wall positioned and joined seamlessly with the wall, this "
"wall is capable of resisting extreme elements as well as hostile forces.  "
"Blast load rated and extremely fire-retardant, breaching it will require "
"specialized tools or an industrial vehicle."
msgstr ""
"コンクリートに似せた模様の壁が、周囲の壁と継ぎ目無く接続されています。この壁は厳しい環境に加えて強い衝撃にも耐性があります。爆風に強く、難燃性も高いため、突破するには特殊な工具か重機が必要です。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "open secret door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"This apparently normal segment of concrete wall has opened to reveal a "
"secret passage."
msgstr "一見何の変哲もないコンクリートの壁が開き、秘密の通路が現れました。"

#. ~ Bashing failed sound
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "thwack!"
msgstr "バシッ！"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "electronic locked metal door"
msgstr "電子ロック付きのドア(金属)"

#. ~ Description of terrain "electronic locked metal door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"An extremely resilient door made of assorted steel, carved and pounded into "
"shape.  It is locked by an electronic keypad."
msgstr "削り出しと鍛造によって成形された合金鋼製の非常に強靭な扉です。キーパッドが付いており、電子錠でロックされています。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "open metal door"
msgstr "開いたドア(金属)"

#. ~ Description of terrain "open metal door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"An extremely resilient door made of assorted steel, carved and pounded into "
"shape.  It's open, so no tools are needed to break in."
msgstr "削り出しと鍛造によって成形された合金鋼製の非常に強靭な扉です。既に開いているため、侵入用の道具は必要ありません。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "open corrugated metal door"
msgstr "開いたドア(トタン板)"

#. ~ Description of terrain "open corrugated metal door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A thin door made of corrugated steel held in a frame.  It's open, so no "
"tools are needed to break in."
msgstr "波状の鉄板を枠に嵌めて作った薄いドアです。既に開いているため、侵入用の道具は必要ありません。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "closed metal door with peephole"
msgstr "ドアスコープ付きの閉じたドア(金属)"

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed metal door with peephole"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"An extremely resilient door made of assorted steel, carved and pounded into "
"shape.  If you examined it more closely, you'd be able to peek through the "
"peephole."
msgstr "削り出しと鍛造によって成形された、合金鋼製の非常に強靭な扉です。近寄って調べると穴から向こう側を覗けます。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "open metal door with peephole"
msgstr "ドアスコープ付きの開いたドア(金属)"

#. ~ Description of terrain "open metal door with peephole"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"An extremely resilient door made of assorted steel, carved and pounded into "
"shape.  If you examined it more closely, you'd be able to peek through the "
"peephole.  No need right now though, since the door is open anyway."
msgstr ""
"削り出しと鍛造によって成形された、非常に強靭な合金鋼製の扉です。近寄って調べると穴から向こう側を覗けます。扉が既に開いているため、わざわざ覗き見る必要はありませんね。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed metal door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A galvanized steel door, forged to withstand punishment and impede anyone or"
" anything.  Typically used in conjunction with automated electronic locking "
"mechanisms that require an external source to unlock."
msgstr ""
"酷使に耐え、あらゆるものの進路を塞ぐ亜鉛メッキ加工された鋼製の扉です。通常は、外部電源で稼働する自動電子ロックシステムと併せて設置されています。"

#. ~ Prying message of terrain "t_door_metal_interior_locked"
#. ~ Prying message of terrain "closed metal door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "You pry open the metal door."
msgstr "ドア(金属)をこじ開けました。"

#. ~ Prying failure of terrain "t_door_metal_interior_locked"
#. ~ Prying failure of terrain "closed metal door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "The metal door is too thick."
msgstr "ドア(金属)が厚すぎてこじ開けられません。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed metal door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"An extremely resilient door made of assorted steel, carved and pounded into "
"shape.  This one has an extra keyhole, so it's likely locked.  You could "
"probably pick the lock."
msgstr ""
"削り出しと鍛造によって成形された合金鋼製の、非常に強靭な扉です。鍵穴が付いており、ロックされている可能性がありますが、ロックピックを使えば開けられそうです。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "closed bar door"
msgstr "閉じたスイングドア"

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed bar door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A detention door made up of crisscrossed stainless steel bars.  The locking "
"mechanism doesn't appear to be engaged."
msgstr "ステンレスの格子が嵌った拘留用の扉です。ロック機構は稼働していないようです。"

#. ~ Hacksaw message of terrain "closed bar door"
#. ~ Hacksaw message of terrain "locked wire gate"
#. ~ Hacksaw message of terrain "closed wire gate"
#. ~ Hacksaw message of terrain "open wire gate"
#. ~ Hacksaw message of terrain "locked retractable gate"
#. ~ Hacksaw message of terrain "closed retractable gate"
#. ~ Hacksaw message of terrain "chain link fence"
#. ~ Hacksaw message of terrain "metal post"
#. ~ Hacksaw message of terrain "railroad track"
#. ~ Hacksaw message of terrain "rebar cage"
#. ~ Hacksaw message of terrain "metal bars"
#. ~ Hacksaw message of terrain "armored boarded up window"
#. ~ Hacksaw message of terrain "window with metal bars"
#. ~ Hacksaw message of terrain "window frame with metal bars"
#. ~ Hacksaw message of terrain "window with metal bars and curtains"
#. ~ Hacksaw message of terrain "window with metal grate"
#. ~ Hacksaw message of terrain "window with metal grate and curtains"
#. ~ Hacksaw message of terrain "prison grating"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-railroads.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-windows.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/maps/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_spaceship.json
msgid "You finish cutting the metal."
msgstr "金属の切断を終えました。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "open bar door"
msgstr "開いたスイングドア"

#. ~ Description of terrain "open bar door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A detention door made up of crisscrossed stainless steel bars.  It's wide "
"open.  Freedom!"
msgstr "ステンレスの格子が嵌った拘留用の扉です。大きく開け放たれています。自由だ！"

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed bar door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A detention door made up of crisscrossed stainless steel bars.  The locking "
"mechanism appears to be engaged.  You could pick it open with enough skill."
msgstr "ステンレスの格子が嵌った拘留用の扉です。ロックされているように見えますが、十分な技能があれば解錠できそうです。"

#. ~ Lockpick message of terrain "closed bar door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "The door swings open…"
msgstr "ドアがゆっくりと開きました..."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "closed frosted glass door"
msgstr "閉じたドア(磨りガラス)"

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed frosted glass door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "A sliding door of frosted white glass."
msgstr "不透明な白いガラス製の引き戸です。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "open frosted glass door"
msgstr "開いたドア(磨りガラス)"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "closed bulkhead door"
msgstr "閉じた隔壁ドア"

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed bulkhead door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"An extremely resilient door made of cast metal, it is watertight and opened "
"using the fly wheel."
msgstr "鍛造によって成形された、非常に強靭な金属扉です。水密性が高く、ハンドルを回転させて開閉します。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "open bulkhead door"
msgstr "開いた隔壁ドア"

#. ~ Description of terrain "open bulkhead door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"An extremely resilient door made of cast metal, it is watertight, or would "
"be if it was closed."
msgstr "鍛造によって成形された、非常に強靭な金属扉です。水密性が高く、閉じた状態で隙間から水が漏れません。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-embrasures.json
msgid "brick wall with embrasure"
msgstr "小窓付きの壁(レンガ)"

#. ~ Description of terrain "brick wall with embrasure"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-embrasures.json
msgid ""
"This brick wall has an embrasure that lets you shoot and use reach weapons "
"against enemies on the outside, while also protecting you."
msgstr "レンガの壁に小窓が付いており、反対側にいる敵に対して射撃や遠距離武器で攻撃しつつ身を守ることができます。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-embrasures.json
msgid "adobe wall with embrasure"
msgstr "小窓付きの壁(日干しレンガ)"

#. ~ Description of terrain "adobe wall with embrasure"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-embrasures.json
msgid ""
"This adobe brick wall has an embrasure that lets you shoot and use reach "
"weapons against enemies on the outside, while also protecting you."
msgstr "日干しレンガの壁に小窓が付いており、反対側にいる敵に対して射撃や遠距離武器で攻撃しつつ身を守ることができます。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-embrasures.json
msgid "stone wall with embrasure"
msgstr "小窓付きの壁(石)"

#. ~ Description of terrain "stone wall with embrasure"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-embrasures.json
msgid ""
"The small opening on this stone wall allows you to shoot and use reach "
"weapons against enemies on the other side, while also providing cover for "
"you."
msgstr "石壁に小窓が付いており、射撃や遠距離武器で向こう側の敵を攻撃しつつ身を守ることができます。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-embrasures.json
msgid "wooden wall with embrasure"
msgstr "小窓付きの壁(木)"

#. ~ Description of terrain "wooden wall with embrasure"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-embrasures.json
msgid ""
"This wooden wall has a hole that lets you shoot and use reach weapons "
"against enemies on the other side.  Highly flammable."
msgstr "木製の壁に小窓が付いており、射撃や遠距離武器で向こう側の敵を攻撃できます。非常に燃えやすい素材で作られています。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-embrasures.json
msgid "wooden wall with a wide opening"
msgstr "穴が開いた壁(木)"

#. ~ Description of terrain "wooden wall with a wide opening"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-embrasures.json
msgid ""
"This wooden wall previously had an embrasure, but the hole has been smashed "
"wide enough that you can climb through it, rendering it kind of pointless.  "
"Highly flammable."
msgstr ""
"以前はこの木製の壁に小窓が開いていたようですが、壊されて出入りできるサイズの大穴になってしまいました。非常に燃えやすい素材で作られています。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-embrasures.json
msgid "log wall with embrasure"
msgstr "小窓付きの壁(丸太)"

#. ~ Description of terrain "log wall with embrasure"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-embrasures.json
msgid ""
"This timber wall has a hole that lets you shoot through and use reach "
"weapons against enemies on the other side, while also protecting you.  Quite"
" flammable."
msgstr "丸太の壁に小窓が付いており、射撃や遠距離武器で向こう側の敵を攻撃しつつ身を守ることができます。燃えやすい素材で作られています。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-embrasures.json
msgid "log wall with a wide opening"
msgstr "穴が開いた壁(丸太)"

#. ~ Description of terrain "log wall with a wide opening"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-embrasures.json
msgid ""
"This timber wall previously had an embrasure, but now the hole is so big "
"that you can climb through it, rendering it kind of pointless.  Quite "
"flammable."
msgstr "以前はこの丸太製の壁に小窓が開いていたようですが、壊されて出入りできるサイズの大穴になってしまいました。燃えやすい素材で作られています。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-embrasures.json
msgid "palisade wall with embrasure"
msgstr "小窓付きの壁(矢来)"

#. ~ Description of terrain "palisade wall with embrasure"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-embrasures.json
msgid ""
"An age-old type of fortification consisting of hefty lumber staked into the "
"ground and cabled together.  This section in particular has an embrasure, so"
" you can shoot or use reach weapons through it while staying safe."
msgstr ""
"分厚い木材を地面に突き立てて繋ぎ合わせた、昔ながらの要塞建築です。この部分には小窓が付いており、射撃や遠距離武器で向こう側の敵を攻撃しつつ身を守ることができます。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-embrasures.json
msgid "simple concrete wall with embrasure"
msgstr "小窓付きの壁(ｺﾝｸﾘｰﾄ)"

#. ~ Description of terrain "simple concrete wall with embrasure"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-embrasures.json
msgid ""
"A durable and uniform concrete wall.  This one has an embrasure, so you can "
"shoot or use reach weapons through it while staying safe."
msgstr "頑丈でむらのないコンクリートの壁です。小窓が付いており、射撃や遠距離武器で向こう側の敵を攻撃しつつ身を守ることができます。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-embrasures.json
msgid "reinforced concrete wall with embrasure"
msgstr "小窓付きの壁(鉄筋ｺﾝｸﾘｰﾄ)"

#. ~ Description of terrain "reinforced concrete wall with embrasure"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-embrasures.json
msgid ""
"A section of wall with a nice small hole, letting you shoot your machine gun"
" from the safety of your reinforced bunker."
msgstr "壁に小窓が付いており、安全な防護壁の内側からマシンガンを発射できます。"

#. ~ Bashing sound
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-embrasures.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/terrain.json
msgid "scrrrash!"
msgstr "ガシャン！"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "palisade gate"
msgstr "門(矢来)"

#. ~ Description of terrain "palisade gate"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid ""
"A large doorway consisting of long logs cabled together, best used as part "
"of a longer wall.  Can act as a door if some type of pulley system were "
"rigged on an adjacent palisade wall."
msgstr "長い丸太を繋げて作った、より長い壁に接続して使う大きな出入口です。壁(矢来)と隣接した位置に滑車装置を設置すれば扉として機能します。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "open palisade gate"
msgstr "開いた門(矢来)"

#. ~ Description of terrain "open palisade gate"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid ""
"A hanging palisade gate, hoisted by a nearby pulley system.  You probably "
"shouldn't be underneath when it comes down."
msgstr "付近の滑車装置によって巻き上げられた状態の吊り橋です。橋を下ろす際に下敷きにならないよう気を付けましょう。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "makeshift portcullis"
msgstr "簡易落とし格子門"

#. ~ Description of terrain "makeshift portcullis"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid ""
"An immense gateway cobbled together from various bits of steel and metal "
"scraps."
msgstr "鉄鋼や金属製の廃材を組み合わせて作った巨大な門です。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "locked wire gate"
msgstr "施錠された門(金網)"

#. ~ Description of terrain "locked wire gate"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid ""
"A gate for a chain link fence.  This one has a locked padlock on the latch "
"system.  With the right tools, you could cut the metal fence or pick the "
"lock.  You could also examine the fence to see if it looks climbable."
msgstr ""
"金網フェンスの門です。掛け金には南京錠が掛かっています。適切な工具を使用すれば金網の切断や南京錠の解錠が可能です。フェンスを調べてよじ登ることもできます。"

#. ~ Boltcut sound of terrain "locked wire gate"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "Gachunk!"
msgstr "ガチャン！"

#. ~ Lockpick message of terrain "locked wire gate"
#. ~ Lockpick message of terrain "locked retractable gate"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "With a satisfying click, the lock on the gate opens."
msgstr "カチッと音がして、門の鍵が開きました。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
msgid "closed wire gate"
msgstr "閉じた門(金網)"

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed wire gate"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
msgid "A gate for a chain link fence with a latch system to stay closed."
msgstr "掛け金が付いた、閉じたままの金網フェンスの門です。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
msgid "open wire gate"
msgstr "開いた門(金網)"

#. ~ Description of terrain "open wire gate"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
msgid ""
"A gate for a chain link fence with a latch system to stay closed.  The latch"
" is undone, so the gate has swung open."
msgstr "掛け金が付いた、閉じたままの金網フェンスの門です。掛け金は外れており、門は開け放たれています。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "locked retractable gate"
msgstr "施錠されたシャッターゲート"

#. ~ Description of terrain "locked retractable gate"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid ""
"A retractable security gate.  The latch on this one is locked.  With the "
"right tools, you could cut the metal fence or disable the lock."
msgstr "施錠された、格納式のセキュリティゲートです。適切な道具を使えば、金属製のフェンスを切断したり、錠を破壊したりして通過できます。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "closed retractable gate"
msgstr "閉じたシャッターゲート"

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed retractable gate"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "A retractable security gate with a latch system to stay closed."
msgstr "施錠システムを備えた格納式のセキュリティゲートです。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "open retractable gate"
msgstr "開いたシャッターゲート"

#. ~ Description of terrain "open retractable gate"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid ""
"A retractable security gate with a latch system to stay closed.  The latch "
"is undone, so the gate has retracted up."
msgstr "施錠システムを備えた格納式のセキュリティゲートです。施錠はされておらず、ゲートは上部に折り畳まれています。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "closed wooden gate"
msgstr "閉じた門(木)"

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed wooden gate"
#. ~ Description of terrain "closed wooden split rail gate"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "A commercial quality gate made of wood with a latch system."
msgstr "一般に流通している掛け金が付いた木製の門です。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "open wooden gate"
msgstr "開いた門(木)"

#. ~ Description of terrain "open wooden gate"
#. ~ Description of terrain "open wooden split rail gate"
#. ~ Description of terrain "open wooden privacy gate"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid ""
"A commercial quality gate made of wood with a latch system.  The gate is "
"wide open, allowing anything to travel through."
msgstr "一般に流通している掛け金が付いた木製の門です。門は開け放たれており、通り抜けられます。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "closed screen door"
msgstr "閉じたドア(網戸)"

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed screen door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "A simple wooden doorway with screen mesh."
msgstr "網戸を取り付けたシンプルな木製の出入り口です。"

#. ~ Bashing sound
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "rattle!"
msgstr "ガシャン！"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "open screen door"
msgstr "開いたドア(網戸)"

#. ~ Description of terrain "open screen door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "A simple wooden doorway with screen mesh.  The door is open."
msgstr "網戸が張られたシンプルな木製の出入り口です。扉は開いています。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "closed chickenwire gate"
msgstr "閉じた門(亀甲金網)"

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed chickenwire gate"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid ""
"A gate for a chickenwire fence with a simple latch system to stay closed."
msgstr "簡単な掛け金が付いた、閉じたままの亀甲金網フェンスの門です。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "open chickenwire gate"
msgstr "開いた門(亀甲金網)"

#. ~ Description of terrain "open chickenwire gate"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid ""
"A gate for a chickenwire fence with a simple latch system to stay closed.  "
"The latch is undone, so the gate has swung open."
msgstr "簡単な掛け金が付いた、閉じたままの亀甲金網フェンスの門です。掛け金は外れており、門は開け放たれています。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "picket fence"
msgstr "柵(棒杭)"

#. ~ Description of terrain "picket fence"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid ""
"A barrier made of wood, it's nothing complicated.  Mildly suggests where not"
" to go."
msgstr "何でもない、木で作られた柵です。通行禁止をやんわりとほのめかしています。"

#. ~ Prying message of terrain "picket fence"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "You pry out the fence post."
msgstr "柵の支柱を引き抜きました。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "woven wattle fence"
msgstr "編み枝フェンス"

#. ~ Description of terrain "woven wattle fence"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "A flimsy barrier made of woven sticks.  Suitable for small animals."
msgstr "木の枝を編んで作った薄っぺらい障壁です。小動物用の囲いに適しています。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "narrow fence posts"
msgstr "柵柱(細枝)"

#. ~ Description of terrain "narrow fence posts"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "A set of narrow wooden posts for a woven wattle fence."
msgstr "編み枝フェンス用の細い木製の支柱です。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
msgid "chain link fence"
msgstr "柵(金網)"

#. ~ Description of terrain "chain link fence"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
msgid ""
"A tall fence made of woven wires.  There aren't any gaps big enough for you "
"to fit through, so you'll have to cut it, climb it, or find a way around."
msgstr "金網が張られた背の高いフェンスです。通れるような隙間はないので、金網を切るか、登って乗り越えるか、回り道を探すしかありません。"

#. ~ Boltcut sound of terrain "chain link fence"
#. ~ Boltcut sound of terrain "wire fence"
#. ~ Boltcut sound of terrain "barbed wire fence"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
msgid "Snick, snick, gachunk!"
msgstr "シャッ、サクッ、ガチャン！"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "metal post"
msgstr "柵柱(金属)"

#. ~ Description of terrain "metal post"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "A set of metal posts that can hold more serious fences."
msgstr "より頑丈な金網を張れる、金属製の支柱です。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "chickenwire fence"
msgstr "柵(亀甲金網)"

#. ~ Description of terrain "chickenwire fence"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid ""
"A tall, rather flimsy fence made of planks and woven wire, suitable for "
"containing small livestock like chickens."
msgstr "木材と捩ったワイヤーで作った、やや脆弱な背の高いフェンスです。鶏などの小型の家畜を囲うのに適しています。"

#. ~ Bashing sound
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "metal rattling!"
msgstr "[金属がガタつく音]"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "screen mesh wall"
msgstr "壁(網戸)"

#. ~ Description of terrain "screen mesh wall"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid ""
"A tall, rather flimsy wall made of planks and screen mesh, suitable for "
"keeping the bugs out."
msgstr "木材と捩ったワイヤーで作った、脆弱な背の高いフェンスです。虫の出入りを防ぐのに適しています。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "chickenwire fence post"
msgstr "柵柱(亀甲金網)"

#. ~ Description of terrain "chickenwire fence post"
#. ~ Description of terrain "fence post"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid ""
"A couple of posts that can support a fence.  They look lonely without the "
"fence."
msgstr "金網を支える支柱です。金網は張られていないようです。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "fence post"
msgstr "柵柱"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "wire fence"
msgstr "柵(ワイヤー)"

#. ~ Description of terrain "wire fence"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid ""
"A barrier made of wire, it's nothing complicated.  Mildly suggests where not"
" to go."
msgstr "何でもない、ワイヤーで作られた障壁です。通行禁止をやんわりとほのめかしています。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "barbed wire fence"
msgstr "鉄条網"

#. ~ Description of terrain "barbed wire fence"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid ""
"A barrier made of sharp barbed wire.  The more persuasive brother of the "
"wire fence."
msgstr "鋭い有刺鉄線でできた障壁です。ワイヤーフェンスの兄弟ですが、こちらの方が強力です。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "rope fence"
msgstr "柵(ロープ)"

#. ~ Description of terrain "rope fence"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid ""
"A barrier made of rope, it's nothing complicated.  Mildly suggests where not"
" to go."
msgstr "何でもない、ロープで作られた障壁です。通行禁止をやんわりとほのめかしています。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "split rail fence"
msgstr "柵(スプリットレール)"

#. ~ Description of terrain "split rail fence"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid ""
"A rather stout fence made of planks and fence posts, suitable for containing"
" livestock like horses, cows and pigs."
msgstr "木材と支柱でできた、やや頑丈なフェンスです。馬、牛、豚などの家畜を囲うのに適しています。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "closed wooden split rail gate"
msgstr "閉じた門(スプリットレール)"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "open wooden split rail gate"
msgstr "開いた門(スプリットレール)"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "metal fence"
msgstr "柵(金属)"

#. ~ Description of terrain "metal fence"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "A simple metal fence."
msgstr "シンプルな金属製の柵です。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "closed metal gate"
msgstr "閉じた門(金属)"

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed metal gate"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "A closed metal gate."
msgstr "閉じた金属製の門です。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "open metal gate"
msgstr "開いた門(金属)"

#. ~ Description of terrain "open metal gate"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "An open metal gate."
msgstr "開いた金属製の門です。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "wooden privacy fence"
msgstr "柵(目隠し)"

#. ~ Description of terrain "wooden privacy fence"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid ""
"A rather stout fence made of planks and fence posts, it is tall enough to "
"prevent people from seeing into your yard."
msgstr "木材と支柱で作った、やや頑丈なフェンスです。背が高いので、庭の目隠しに最適です。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "closed wooden privacy gate"
msgstr "閉じた目隠し門"

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed wooden privacy gate"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid ""
"A commercial quality gate made of wood with a latch system.  It is tall "
"enough to prevent people from seeing into your yard."
msgstr "掛け金で閉鎖できる、市販の木製ゲートです。背が高いので、庭の目隠しに最適です。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "open wooden privacy gate"
msgstr "開いた目隠し門"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "railing"
msgstr "手すり"

#. ~ Description of terrain "railing"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "A section of wooden railing."
msgstr "木製の手すりです。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "glass railing"
msgstr "手すり(ガラス)"

#. ~ Description of terrain "glass railing"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "A section of railing made out of glass."
msgstr "ガラス製の手すりです。"

#. ~ Bashing sound
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "glass braking!"
msgstr "[ガラスが割れる大きな音！]"

#. ~ Bashing failed sound
#. ~ Bashing sound
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
#: data/mods/MindOverMatter/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_tanks.json
msgid "ker-rash!"
msgstr "ガッシャーン！"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "metal railing"
msgstr "手すり(金属)"

#. ~ Description of terrain "metal railing"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "A section of metal railing."
msgstr "金属製の手すりです。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "concrete railing"
msgstr "手すり(ｺﾝｸﾘｰﾄ)"

#. ~ Description of terrain "concrete railing"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "A section of cemented concrete railing."
msgstr "コンクリート製の手すりです。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "guard rail"
msgstr "ガードレール"

#. ~ Description of terrain "guard rail"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid ""
"A section of metal railing, put in place to prevent people from falling or "
"taking the easy way out."
msgstr "金属製の手すりです。道路外への落下や侵入を防ぐために設置されています。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid "cattle feeder"
msgstr "飼料桶"

#. ~ Description of terrain "cattle feeder"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
msgid ""
"A section of tall steel with a solid base and feed spaces above to allow "
"livestock to reach the contained food."
msgstr "頑丈な土台の上に背の高いスチール製の箱が乗っており、供給した餌を家畜が食べられる仕組みになっています。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flesh.json
msgid "overgrown floor"
msgstr "床(肥大した肉)"

#. ~ Description of terrain "overgrown floor"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flesh.json
msgid ""
"A bare concrete floor, almost completely covered by twitching filaments of "
"gray flesh."
msgstr "剥き出しのコンクリート床は、繊毛を揺らめかせる灰色の肉に覆われています。"

#. ~ Bashing sound
#. ~ Snippet in category "<random_sound>"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flesh.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fungal.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-triffid.json
#: data/json/snippets/snippets.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/maps/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_habitat_floor.json
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/furniture.json
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_druid.json
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/terrain.json data/mods/No_Hope/terrain.json
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/furniture_and_terrain/furniture.json
msgid "SMASH!"
msgstr "ガシャン！"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flesh.json
msgid "overgrown wall"
msgstr "壁(肥大した肉)"

#. ~ Description of terrain "overgrown wall"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flesh.json
msgid ""
"A concrete wall overgrown by a grotesque grid of veins and knotted flesh."
msgstr "コンクリートの壁は、血管や瘤が生えたグロテスクな肉の網に覆われています。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "concrete floor"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
msgid ""
"A bare and cold concrete floor that can support a roof, could still insulate"
" from the outdoors but roof collapse is possible if supporting walls are "
"broken down."
msgstr ""
"上層の屋根を支えられる剥き出しの冷たいコンクリート床です。屋外からの熱を遮断しますが、支えとなる壁が破壊されると屋根が崩壊する可能性があります。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "concrete floor"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
msgid ""
"A bare and cold concrete floor with a streak of yellow paint, could still "
"insulate from the outdoors but roof collapse is possible if supporting walls"
" are broken down."
msgstr ""
"屋根と同じ素材で作られた、黄色いペンキで塗ってある剥き出しの冷たいコンクリート床です。断熱効果がありますが、支えている壁が破壊されると屋根が崩壊する可能性があります。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "concrete floor"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
msgid ""
"A bare and cold concrete floor with a streak of red paint, could still "
"insulate from the outdoors but roof collapse is possible if supporting walls"
" are broken down."
msgstr ""
"屋根と同じ素材で作られた、赤いペンキで塗ってある剥き出しの冷たいコンクリート床です。断熱効果がありますが、支えている壁が破壊されると屋根が崩壊する可能性があります。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "concrete floor"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
msgid ""
"A bare and cold concrete floor with painted stripes of black and yellow, "
"could still insulate from the outdoors but roof collapse is possible if "
"supporting walls are broken down."
msgstr ""
"屋根と同じ素材で作られた、黒色と黄色の縞模様に塗られた剥き出しの冷たいコンクリート床です。断熱効果がありますが、支えている壁が破壊されると屋根が崩壊する可能性があります。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "concrete floor"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
msgid ""
"A bare and cold concrete floor with a streak of yellow paint and a still-"
"functioning light attached to the ceiling above, could still insulate from "
"the outdoors but roof collapse is possible if supporting walls are broken "
"down."
msgstr ""
"黄色いペンキで塗ってある剥き出しの冷たいコンクリート床です。天井に取り付けられた照明は、今も機能しています。断熱効果がありますが、支えている壁が破壊されると屋根が崩壊する可能性があります。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
msgid "concrete floor, overhead light"
msgstr "床(ｺﾝｸﾘｰﾄ)と天井灯"

#. ~ Description of terrain "concrete floor, overhead light"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
msgid ""
"A bare and cold concrete floor with a still-functioning light attached to "
"the ceiling above."
msgstr "剥き出しの冷たいコンクリート床です。上部の天井に取り付けられた照明は、今も機能しています。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
msgid "wooden floor, overhead light"
msgstr "床(木)と天井灯"

#. ~ Description of terrain "wooden floor, overhead light"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
msgid ""
"Interlocking wooden tiles that are more than likely treated against fire, "
"with a still-functioning light attached to the ceiling above."
msgstr "防火性能が高そうな木製タイルを組み合わせた床です。上部の天井に取り付けられた照明は、今も機能しています。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
msgid "brick floor"
msgstr "床(レンガ)"

#. ~ Description of terrain "brick floor"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
msgid ""
"A relatively flat area made of tightly placed bricks.  Can support a roof."
msgstr "レンガが敷き詰められた比較的平らな床です。上層の屋根を支えられます。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
msgid "dirt floor, overhead light"
msgstr "床(土)と天井灯"

#. ~ Description of terrain "dirt floor, overhead light"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
msgid ""
"A floor consisting of finely mixed earth that has been tamped down, with a "
"still-functioning light attached to the ceiling above."
msgstr "目の細かい土を押し固めて作った床です。上部の天井に取り付けられた照明は、今も機能しています。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
msgid "metal floor, with overhead light"
msgstr "床(金属)と天井灯"

#. ~ Description of terrain "metal floor, with overhead light"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
msgid ""
"High-quality and tough checkered metal flooring to reduce the risk of slips "
"and falls, with a still-functioning light attached to the ceiling above."
msgstr ""
"スリップや転倒のリスクを軽減する、高品質で強靭な金属でできた格子模様のフローリングです。上部の天井に取り付けられた照明は、今も機能しています。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
msgid "strong concrete floor, overhead light"
msgstr "床(強化ｺﾝｸﾘｰﾄ)と天井灯"

#. ~ Description of terrain "strong concrete floor, overhead light"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
msgid ""
"An extremely resilient floor made from carefully placed rebar and poured "
"concrete, with a still-functioning light attached to the ceiling above."
msgstr "規則正しく並べた鉄筋にコンクリートを流し込んで作った、非常に強靭な床です。上部の天井に取り付けられた照明は、今も機能しています。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
msgid "gray linoleum floor, overhead light"
msgstr "床(リノリウム)と天井灯"

#. ~ Description of terrain "gray linoleum floor, overhead light"
#. ~ Description of terrain "white linoleum floor, overhead light"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
msgid ""
"Linoleum flooring with a still-functioning light attached to the ceiling "
"above."
msgstr "リノリウムの床です。上部の天井に取り付けられた照明は、今も機能しています。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
msgid "white linoleum floor, overhead light"
msgstr "天井に照明が取り付けられた、白いリノリウムの床です。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
msgid "small rebar roof cage"
msgstr "鉄筋骨組(小さな屋根)"

#. ~ Description of terrain "small rebar roof cage"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
msgid ""
"A series of structural supports crafted from rebar in order to allow the "
"pouring of concrete for a more stable floor and roof support."
msgstr "コンクリートを流し込むことで頑丈な床となり、上層の屋根も支えられるようになる、鉄筋製の構造支持材です。"

#. ~ Bashing sound
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
msgid "SCRRRASH!"
msgstr "ガシャーン！"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/maps/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_habitat_floor.json
msgid "reinforced concrete floor"
msgstr "床(鉄筋ｺﾝｸﾘｰﾄ)"

#. ~ Description of terrain "reinforced concrete floor"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
msgid ""
"An extremely resilient floor made from carefully placed rebar and poured "
"concrete, capable of providing protection from the elements.  It can support"
" a roof, but that still requires supporting walls, otherwise it may very "
"well cave in."
msgstr ""
"規則正しく並べた鉄筋にコンクリートを注入して作られた、風雨を防ぐ非常に頑丈な床です。上層の屋根を支えられますが、隣接する壁が破壊されると屋根が崩落する可能性があります。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
msgid "fractured concrete floor"
msgstr "割れた床(ｺﾝｸﾘｰﾄ)"

#. ~ Description of terrain "fractured concrete floor"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
msgid ""
"Thin strands of violet light shimmer in the air above this concrete floor, "
"like cracks upon a pane of glass.  It can support a roof."
msgstr "コンクリート床の表面から立ち昇るように、ひび割れたガラスにも似た細い紫色の光の筋がきらめいています。上層の屋根を支えられます。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
msgid "rebar roof cage"
msgstr "鉄筋骨組(屋根)"

#. ~ Description of terrain "rebar roof cage"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
msgid ""
"A network of architecturally sound rebar in order to support a floor and "
"roof support, looks like it's missing the poured concrete."
msgstr "床と屋根を支えるための頑丈そうな鉄筋構造ですが、まだコンクリートが注入されていないようです。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
msgid "half-built reinforced concrete floor"
msgstr "建設途中の床(鉄筋ｺﾝｸﾘｰﾄ)"

#. ~ Description of terrain "half-built reinforced concrete floor"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
msgid ""
"An unfinished construction of rebar and poured concrete; the floor hasn't "
"been smoothed and the roof support isn't quite filled in yet."
msgstr "鉄筋の隙間にコンクリートを注いだだけの、未完成の床です。表面は滑らかになっておらず、上層の屋根も十分に支えられません。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
#: data/mods/No_Hope/terrain.json
msgid "rock floor"
msgstr "床(岩石)"

#. ~ Description of terrain "rock floor"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
msgid ""
"A relatively flat area of rock and stone.  Looks stable enough to be mined "
"with the proper mining gear.  Can support a roof."
msgstr "比較的平坦な岩石の床です。脆さは感じられず、適切な道具があれば掘削できそうです。上層の屋根を支えられます。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
msgid "marble floor"
msgstr "床(大理石)"

#. ~ Description of terrain "marble floor"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
msgid ""
"A smooth and flat flooring made of marble tiles.  Beautiful and expensive.  "
"Can support a roof."
msgstr "大理石タイルでできた滑らかで平らな床です。美しく、かつ高価です。上層の屋根を支えられます。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
msgid "warped stone floor"
msgstr "歪んだ床"

#. ~ Description of terrain "warped stone floor"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
msgid ""
"A rough stone floor.  Its patterns constantly shift as if your mind can't "
"quite understand what it's really seeing.  Can support a roof."
msgstr "きめの粗い石の床です。模様が常に変化しており、見つめていると自分の視覚が信用できなくなります。上層の屋根を支えられます。"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "metal floor"
msgstr "床(金属)"

#. ~ Description of terrain "metal floor"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
msgid ""
"High-quality and tough checkered metal flooring to reduce the risk of slips "
"and falls.  Can support a roof."
msgstr "スリップや転倒の危険性を軽減する、高品質で強靭な金属でできた格子模様の床です。上層の屋根を支えられます。"

#. ~ Bashing sound
#. ~ Bashing failed sound
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-liquids.json
