msgstr "卵の酢漬けです。少々塩辛いですが美味しく食べられ、長持ちします。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/egg.json
msgid "curing roe"
msgid_plural "curing roe"
msgstr[0] "魚卵(脱水中)"

#. ~ Description of "curing roe"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/egg.json
msgid ""
"Roe in the process of becoming fully cured with salt, capable of becoming "
"homemade caviar.  The flavor is slowly developing at this stage, and is "
"currently significantly unpleasant due to the residual salt.  Activate it "
"once completed to make use of the final product."
msgstr ""
"塩で漬けて脱水している途中の魚卵です。水が抜ける段階でゆっくりと風味が増しますが、今の状態では塩味が強すぎて美味しくありません。脱水が完了した状態で使用すると、自家製キャビアが完成します。"

#. ~ "msg" action message of item "curing roe"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/egg.json
msgid "You remove the roe from the brine and now have post apocalypse caviar."
msgstr "塩水から魚卵を取り出し、滅亡世界のキャビアが完成したことを確認しました。"

#. ~ "not_ready_msg" action message of item "curing roe"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/egg.json
msgid "The roe isn't fully cured yet."
msgstr "魚卵はまだ硬くなっていません。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/egg.json
msgid "post apocalyptic 'caviar'"
msgid_plural "post apocalyptic 'caviar'"
msgstr[0] "自家製キャビア"

#. ~ Description of "post apocalyptic 'caviar'"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/egg.json
msgid ""
"Fish eggs that have been cured in a salty brine.  Can be vacuum sealed to "
"preserve freshness.  Technically caviar only came from a specific type of "
"Sturgeon roe but the FDA allows all cured fish to be referred to as caviar."
msgstr ""
"塩水の中で熟成させた魚卵です。密封しておけば鮮度が長持ちします。専門的に言えば、キャビアとは特定種のチョウザメの卵からしか作れませんが、FDAは脱水した魚卵であれば魚種は何であれキャビアと呼ぶことを許可しています。"

