"\n"
"Made of hardened steel and with a molded grip that fits your hand perfectly, this weapon looks as good as any you might find in a museum.  The balance is perfect and the edge is as sharp as a razor."
msgstr ""
"ドイツで生まれた、両手持ち用の湾曲した長い片刃剣です。ロングソードよりは洗練されていませんが、切れ味が衰えにくく安価なため、ヨーロッパ全土に普及しました。\n"
"\n"
"刃全体が焼入炭素鋼で作られており、柄の形状は手によく馴染みます。武器全体のバランスも完璧で、刃は鋭く研がれています。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid "tempered steel kriegsmesser"
msgid_plural "tempered steel kriegsmessers"
msgstr[0] "クリークスメッサー(焼戻炭素鋼)"

#. ~ Description of "tempered steel kriegsmesser"
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid ""
"A single-edged two-handed sword of German design, with a long, curved blade.  It became popular across Europe due to its low cost while maintaining strong cutting power in comparison to the more sophisticated longsword.\n"
"\n"
"Made of tempered steel, this is a masterpiece.  The grip, the balance, the blade, all perfect.  This is the peak of the swordsmith's craft."
msgstr ""
"ドイツで生まれた、両手持ち用の湾曲した長い片刃剣です。ロングソードよりは洗練されていませんが、切れ味が衰えにくく安価なため、ヨーロッパ全土に普及しました。\n"
"\n"
"刃全体が焼戻炭素鋼で作られており、柄のフィット感、全体のバランス、刃の切れ味、全てにおいて完璧です。これぞ匠の技の結晶です。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid "falx"
msgid_plural "falxes"
msgstr[0] "ファルクス"

#. ~ Description of "falx"
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid ""
"A distinct Dacian sword that curves forward, allowing you to bypass shields "
"or hook and pull enemies, while delivering decent chopping damage."
msgstr "ダキア人だけが使っていた、前方に湾曲している剣です。盾を避けたり敵を引き倒したりしながら、切り刻むようにダメージを与えられます。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid "mild steel falx"
msgid_plural "mild steel falxes"
msgstr[0] "ファルクス(低炭素鋼)"

#. ~ Description of "mild steel falx"
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid ""
"A distinct Dacian sword that curves forward, allowing you to bypass shields or hook and pull enemies, while delivering decent chopping damage.\n"
"\n"
"Made with mild steel and lacking a proper grip, this is better than the sticks you swung around as a kid, but you know you can do better."
msgstr ""
