#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/criminal_1.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/criminal_1.json
msgid "Lucky you.  How did you get away?"
msgstr "運がよかったな。どうやって逃げたんだ？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/criminal_1.json
msgid ""
"It was just <swear> chaos on the streets, man.  But I'm used to chaos.  You "
"don't live as long as I've lived and not know how to keep away from a fight "
"you can't win.  Biggest worry wasn't the zombies and the monsters, honestly."
"  But I swear, some cops got a nightstick so far up their ass…  I didn't "
"have time to ditch my orange when stuff kept swipin' at me, and I swear, "
"cops got a look at me, they decided I was the big problem.  Goddamn walking "
"corpse next to me, who do they pick to shoot at?  Pricks."
msgstr ""
"通りは、<swear>、酷い混乱だったよ。でも、混乱には慣れっこさ。あんたでは私より長生きできないだろうし、勝てない戦いを避ける方法も分からないだろう。一番の気がかりはゾンビや化け物じゃない。誓っていうが、何人かの警官は、既におかしな状態で警棒を振り回してた...こっちが囚人服をどこかへ捨てるより、奴らが向かってくる方が早かった。警官たちはこっちを睨みつけ、襲い掛かって来たんだ、本当だ。動く死体がすぐ傍まで来てたのに、何でこっちが狙われるんだ？糞共め。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/criminal_1.json
msgid "How did you keep from getting arrested?"
msgstr "どうやって逮捕されずに過ごしてきたんだ？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/criminal_1.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/criminal_1.json
msgid "What were you in for in the first place?"
msgstr "そもそも何の罪を犯したんだ？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/CleverRaven/Cataclysm-
#. DDA/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/criminal_1.json
msgctxt "npc:f"
msgid ""
"'cuz I know how cops think.  If you can call it that.  Early days, they were"
" still going after alarms in case it meant, I dunno, survivors.  You smack "
"some fucker's sports car, it starts wailing, the cops come to take a look "
"and you can walk right behind 'em.  That's the thing about cops; they follow"
" orders, right?  Even when the world's comin' apart.  I kept my head down "
"until I got past the worst of it, but then, lucky me, I got sergeant "
"brainiac.  Figured out why someone would trip an alarm on purpose, had them "
"case all up and down the streets for me.  I wound up on the edge of town "
"layin' low under an abandoned RV for a few hours.  By then… well, they had "
"some other big problems to deal with.  For a little bit.  Might've survived "
"if they hadn't blown their wads chasing me around the block."
msgstr ""
"警察の考えが分かるからだ。ちょっと大げさな言い方だったかな。大変動が始まった頃、あいつらは生存者が残ってることを期待して、街の警報に気を付けてた。いけ好かない誰かのスポーツカーをぶち壊せば、車はビービー騒ぎ出して、警官が様子を見に来る。その背後でこっそり動けば完璧。警察ってそういうもんなのさ。いっつも命令に従う、そうだろ？世界が終わっても変わらないんだ。最悪の事態を乗り越えるまではこっそり動いてたが、そこで幸運にも、頭脳派の奴がやってきた。そいつはわざと警報を作動させる理由を突き留めたのか、通りにある車の警報を片っ端から鳴らして回って、警官たちを翻弄したんだ。騒ぎが起きてる数時間は、街はずれに放置されてたキャンピングカーにじっと籠ってた。しばらくは...そうだな、警官は仕事が増えて大変だったろうな。多少は同情するよ。私を追ってゾンビの群れとかち合ってなければ、生き延びられたかもしれないのに。"

