#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
msgid ""
"A contractor?  How much does something like a survivalist shelter cost?"
msgstr "業者？こういうシェルターを建てるには、費用がいくらかかるんだ？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
msgid ""
"But we're good to go, right?  I mean… the door is the only trick you had?  "
"No clever traps hidden in the walls or anything?"
msgstr "でも、仕掛けさえ分かれば簡単に入れたな？つまり...ドア以外に仕掛けは用意していないのか？壁に卑劣な罠を隠しておくとか、そういうのは？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
msgid ""
"You wouldn't keep ALL your tricks and secrets from me, though, would you?  "
"After everything we've been through?"
msgstr "私に仕掛けを隠しておく意味は、もうないんじゃないかな？ここも共有することになるんだろう？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
msgid "That's all I wanted to know."
msgstr "今聞きたいことはそれだけだ。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/CleverRaven/Cataclysm-
#. DDA/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
msgctxt "npc:f"
msgid ""
"Nope, that's it.  Got the idea for the door from a book on medieval castles,"
" in case you were wondering.  But instead of a counterweight holding a "
"drawbridge up, I just ram a hex key in a hole."
msgstr ""
"ああ、それだけだよ。ちなみに、ドアのアイデアは中世の城の本から拝借したんだ。おもりで跳ね橋を上げておく仕掛けを、六角棒スパナで代用したってわけさ。"

