msgstr "[4 ﾏｰﾁ] 分かった、はいどうぞ。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Fatima_Al_Jadir.json
msgid "[3 merch] All right, here's your money."
msgstr "[3 ﾏｰﾁ] 分かった、はいどうぞ。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Fatima_Al_Jadir.json
msgid "[BARTER] Come on, I'm serious here."
msgstr "[交渉] 頼むよ、真剣に頼んでいるんだ。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Fatima_Al_Jadir.json
msgid ""
"[BARTER] That's still pretty steep, I risked my neck out there for your "
"book.  Can't you manage a little lower?"
msgstr "[交渉] ちょっと高額すぎるよ。危険を冒して本をもってきてあげたんだ。もう少し安くならないか？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Fatima_Al_Jadir.json
msgid ""
"Hey, I appreciate that, but I know what I've got, and I can make good money "
"with that time.  Sorry, my price stands."
msgstr ""
"ああ、それについては感謝してるよ。でも、私は自分の取り柄を把握できてるし、あなたに教える時間で他の仕事をすれば結構な額を稼げるの。申し訳ないけど、安くはできない。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Fatima_Al_Jadir.json
msgid ""
"Oh, fine, you weasel.  I suppose I can manage for 3 notes.  I seriously "
"can't go lower though, we'll be using up my resources and time and I gotta "
"pay for the gas and the food somehow."
msgstr ""
"もう、分かったよ、ズルいなぁ。マーチ3枚にしよう。でも、これ以上は本当に値下げできない。資源や時間に余裕がないから、ガソリンや食べ物を買う分を稼がないといけないんだ。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Fatima_Al_Jadir.json
msgid ""
"I was on my way to visit my parents back in Burlington, waiting at a bus station, when the evacuation notices started sounding.  I'd been a little out of touch for a bit and didn't realize how bad the rioting was getting.  When my bus arrived it got repurposed into an evacuation vehicle, and took me here.  I… I didn't used to be very religious, it's just something I was born to, but since this happened I've been thinking a lot more about God, and how grateful I am for His help in surviving.  With things still so difficult, it helps to know He's got some plan for me.\n"
"\n"
"Anyway, mine was the second bus to arrive, and they were just getting some triage and processing stuff set up.  I was put in charge of helping with the wounded, along with Uyen.  Things went a little strange later on… one of the women doing triage and processing had a bit of a hang-up about particular, um, colors of people being allowed into the center.  She claimed to have lost our 'papers', along with a lot of other peoples'.  Thankfully because we'd helped so many we were able to argue that they couldn't leave us out, but there was no space left downstairs by the time we got that sorted, so here we are."
msgstr ""
"避難警報が鳴り始めた時は、バーリントンにいる両親を訪ねるために、バス停にいたんだ。世間の事情にはちょっと疎かったから、暴動がどれだけ激化してるかなんて気付かなかった。到着したバスは避難用車両に転用されていて、それに乗ってここに着いた。その...私は生まれた頃からあまり信心深い方じゃなかったけど、こんな事があってからは神について深く考えるようになった。神の助けがあって生き延びられたんだと思って感謝してるよ。状況は今も厳しいけど、きっと何とかなると思う。\n"
"\n"
"さて、私が乗ったバスは2番目に到着したみたいで、スタッフがトリアージや治療の準備をしていた。私はホェンと一緒に、負傷者を介助して回ってた。そこでちょっと厄介な事があって...トリアージと避難手続きを担当していた女の人が、ええと、特定の肌の色の人をセンターに入れたくなかったみたいで、ちょっと変な状況になったんだ。彼女は私たちのも含めた『手続き書類』を紛失したって言い出してね。私たちはずっと応急処置を手伝ってたから、避難センター内へ入れるようスタッフに取り計らってもらえた。でも、列に並んだ時点で階下にはもうスペースがなかったから、ここに留まっているんだ。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Fatima_Al_Jadir.json
msgid ""
"Things are still tense, but I've been busy lately.  Jenny's had her project "
"going and got me started helping her out with it, and for some reason that "
"seems to have been the tipping point: I'm getting chances to do a lot more "
"welding work now.  It's helping.  I feel a bit self-conscious praying in the"
" common areas, and of course, we don't go outside if we can help it."
msgstr ""
"状況は良くなってはいないけど、最近忙しくなってきたんだ。ジェニーが進めてるプロジェクトを手伝い始めたの。それが転機だったのかな。今では、もっとたくさんの溶接作業をする機会ができてね。仕事がはかどってるよ。共用スペースで祈るのはちょっと恥ずかしいし、当然助けがないと外には出られないけど。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Fatima_Al_Jadir.json
msgid ""
"It's tense here.  I know I'd feel a lot better if I had something to do with"
" my skills, or even if I just had a quiet place to pray sometimes.  I feel a"
" bit self-conscious praying in the common areas.  Jenny was talking about "
"some project ideas she had that could get me doing my job again, but I admit"
" I'm pretty nervous about going outside."
msgstr ""
"ここはピリピリしてる。自分の技能を活かせる仕事が見つかるか、静かに祈る場所があれば、もう少し穏やかに過ごせるんだけどね。公共のスペースで祈るのはちょっと照れ臭いんだ。ジェニーが私の技能を役立てられるプロジェクトがあるって話してくれたけど、外に出るのはどうしても緊張するな。"

#. ~ Mission name
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Fatima_Al_Jadir.json
msgid "Find a copy of the Quran"
msgstr "本(一般/コーラン)を持ってくる"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find a copy of the Quran"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Fatima_Al_Jadir.json
msgid "I could use a bit of help to find a copy of the Quran."
msgstr "コーランを探すのを手伝ってもらえないかな。"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find a copy of the Quran"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Fatima_Al_Jadir.json
msgid ""
"I feel silly asking this, but here goes.  I've never been really into "
"reading holy books and stuff like that.  I usually went to the mosque on "
"Friday, and I try to pray five times a day but I hardly ever manage it.  I "
"guess I'm not a very good Muslim, but with all that's happened I would "
"really love to have a copy of the Quran to read.  This seems like a time to "
"get back in touch with God, you know?"
msgstr ""
"こんなことを頼むのも申し訳ないんだけど、聞いて。私は聖典なんて今まで全然興味が無かったんだ。金曜日はいつもモスクへ行って、一日5回祈ってたけど、聖典を自分で読むことは滅多になかった。私は良いイスラム教徒ではないんだろうけど、こんな経験をしてからは、コーランを手元に置きたいと心から思うようになったの。これは神の教えに触れ直すいい機会なんじゃないかな？"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find a copy of the Quran"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Fatima_Al_Jadir.json
msgid "Thank you.  I'll see if I can save up a little reward for you."
msgstr "ありがとう。少しでもお礼を渡せるよう準備しておくよ。"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find a copy of the Quran"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Fatima_Al_Jadir.json
msgid "That's okay.  Thanks for offering."
msgstr "分かった。話を聞いてくれてありがとう。"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find a copy of the Quran"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Fatima_Al_Jadir.json
msgid ""
"It's not as common as the bible, but you should be able to find copies in "
"most libraries and bookstores, or in religious buildings.  Make sure you get"
" the translated version, I can't read Arabic!"
msgstr "聖書ほどは見かけないけど、大抵の図書館や書店、あとは宗教施設に置いてあるはず。翻訳版を持ってきてよ。私はアラビア語が読めないからね！"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find a copy of the Quran"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Fatima_Al_Jadir.json
msgid ""
"Thank you so much.  Just having a copy to keep at hand does actually feel "
"pretty comforting.  I did a few extra rounds of chores and saved the "
"proceeds for if you managed this, here you go.  It's not much but I hope it "
"helps."
msgstr ""
"本当にありがとう。手元に置いておけるだけで、すごく心が安らいだ気がするよ。私も雑用をいくつかこなして、お礼を用意した。さあどうぞ。豪華じゃないけど、役に立つといいな。"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find a copy of the Quran"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Fatima_Al_Jadir.json
msgid ""
"It's okay.  I don't know how much comfort I'd have found in an old book "
"anyway."
msgstr "そう。別に、そんな古い本で心が休まるとも思ってないし、気にしないで。"

#. ~ Unique name of a male NPC
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Garry_Villeneuve.json
msgid "Garry Villeneuve"
msgstr "ｷﾞｬﾘｰ ﾋﾞﾙﾇｰﾌﾞ"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Garry_Villeneuve.json
msgid ""
"*looks up at you with a gaunt face.  His loose clothes and sharp cheekbones "
"suggest he recently lost a lot of weight.  \"Hi.  Hi there.\"  He scratches "
"at a patchy beard of gray stubble.  \"I'm Garry, Garry Villeneuve.\""
msgstr ""
"*はやつれた顔でこちらを見ています。だぶついた服と窪んだ頬を見れば、最近急激に体重を落としたことが分かります。「や、やあ、どうも。」挨拶しながら彼は、白髪交じりの無精ひげを掻きました。「私はギャリー、ギャリー・ビルヌーブだ。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Garry_Villeneuve.json
msgid "Nice to meet you, Garry."
msgstr "はじめまして、ギャリー。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Garry_Villeneuve.json
msgid "Hi Garry, nice to meet you.  I gotta go though."
msgstr "やぁギャリー、ごきげんよう。悪いけどもう行くよ。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Garry_Villeneuve.json
msgid "*smiles at you briefly.  He looks like he hasn't been eating well.  \""
msgstr "*は弱々しく微笑みました。あまり食事を摂っていないようです。「"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Garry_Villeneuve.json
msgid "Well, hello."
msgstr "ああ、こんにちは。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Garry_Villeneuve.json
msgid "Hi, Garry.  What's up?"
msgstr "やあ、ギャリー。調子はどう？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Garry_Villeneuve.json
msgid "Hi Garry.  I can't stay to talk."
msgstr "やあギャリー。話は後にしよう。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Garry_Villeneuve.json
msgid "Nice to meet you too.  Are you staying here, or something?"
msgstr "こちらこそ。君はここで生活するのか？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Garry_Villeneuve.json
msgid "No, I'm a traveler.  What's up with you?"
msgstr "いいや、通りがかっただけだ。調子はどう？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Garry_Villeneuve.json
msgid "Nope, in fact I'm leaving right now."
msgstr "いや、もう行かないと。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Garry_Villeneuve.json
msgid ""
"Doing my best to keep going in the face of… everything.  Not getting far."
msgstr "折れないように全力を尽くしている...あらゆることにね。前に進めているとは思えないけど。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Garry_Villeneuve.json
msgid ""
"Before the apocalypse I was an electrician.  Boris here is my brother-in-"
"law, and we were a decent contractor team.  When the evacuations sounded, we"
" left together with our…\" he swallows and coughs before continuing, \"with "
"our families.  We got stuck into a crowded evac shelter, then onto a crowded"
" bus.  Then… everything went wrong.  The bus was attacked, destroyed.  "
"Nearly everyone died.  A few of us made it back… not enough."
msgstr ""
"大変動が起きる前は電気技師をしていた。ここにいる義理の弟のボリスと2人で、立派に請負業をこなしていたんだ。避難警報が鳴った時、私たちは...」彼は唾をのみ、咳ばらいをしてから話を続けました。「家族と一緒に避難した。混雑した避難所に詰め込まれ、そこから混雑したバスに乗り込んだ。それからは...何もかも上手く行かなかった。バスが攻撃を受けて破壊され、ほぼ全員が死んだ。何人かは生き返ったけど...あれじゃ何の意味もない。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Garry_Villeneuve.json
msgid "You lost someone…"
msgstr "誰かを亡くしたのか..."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Garry_Villeneuve.json
msgid ""
"Yes.  My wife, Linda… thrown from the bus.  She didn't make it.  And… and my"
" nephew, Ash, Boris and Stan's son.  We got him here, but there wasn't "
"anything we could do.\"  He gestures for a moment as if trying to explain it"
" without words, then shrugs.  \"Internal injuries."
msgstr ""
"ああ。妻のリンダは...バスの外へ投げ出された。助けられなかった。それから...ボリスとスタンの息子で、私の甥にあたるアッシュだ。ここまで連れては来たが、手の施しようがなかった。」彼は身振りで説明しようとしましたが、肩をすくめ、話を続けました。「内臓の傷が酷くてね。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Garry_Villeneuve.json
msgid "Do you want to tell me about Linda?"
msgstr "リンダについて聞いてもいいか？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Garry_Villeneuve.json
msgid "Tell me about Ash."
msgstr "アッシュについて聞きたい。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Garry_Villeneuve.json
msgid ""
"*looks unsure, then sighs softly.  \"I don't know what to say.  She was my "
"second wife; my first wife passed away about fifteen years ago.  I've gone "
"through this before, and it was bad enough then.\"  He stares at the floor "
"for a moment.  \"We don't have any touchstones anymore, you know?  I've got "
"Boris and Stan, but they can't support me, and what else is there?\"  He "
"looks back up at you, appearing to remember the conversation.  \"Sorry, you "
"were asking about Linda.  She was wonderful, always surprising me.  One of "
"those people you just couldn't predict, so much fun and full of life.  "
"Really into rock climbing.  I always used to be afraid she'd hurt herself in"
" a climbing accident.\"  He laughs, a single harsh sound more like a cough."
"  \"Funny how life throws you curveballs.\""
msgstr ""
"*は自信なさげに小さくため息をつきました。「私の後妻だ。最初の妻は15年ほど前に他界した。その時も似たような、酷い気分だった。」じっと床を見つめながら、言葉を絞り出しています。「支柱が折れたみたいだ。ボリスとスタンは、私を支えてはくれない。いったいどうすればいい？」ギャリーはこちらの存在を今まで忘れていたかのように我に返り、話を続けました。「失礼、リンダの話だったな。素晴らしい人だった。いつも私を驚かせてくれた。ロッククライミングが大好きで、事故で怪我をするんじゃないかと、私はいつも心配していた。」そして彼は、咳き込むように苦し気に笑いました。「まさしく運命のいたずらだな。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Garry_Villeneuve.json
msgid ""
"*smiles for a moment, his face returning to what it must have looked like "
"before everything.  \"God, that kid was funny.  Such a little nerd.  He'd "
"come bombing into any conversation to interrupt and tell you about whatever "
"his latest obsession was, didn't matter what else was going on.  We'd have "
"to remind him to go to the bathroom sometimes.\"  Garry looks around, "
"swallowing hard for a second, and wipes his hands across his face.  \"It's "
"so damn quiet here without him.\""
msgstr ""
"*の顔にすぐさま笑みが浮かびました。以前はそのように自然に笑えていたのでしょう。「ああ、本当に面白い子でね。まるで小さなオタクだ。どんな話にも割り込んできて、最近夢中になっている事などを聞かせてくれる。あまりに一生懸命話すものだから、そろそろトイレに行っておけと、時々言ってやらなきゃいけない。」そこまで話すと、ギャリーは周囲を見回し、唾を呑み、両手で顔を覆いました。「あの子がいないと、とても静かだ。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Garry_Villeneuve.json
msgid ""
"It's tense here, but I don't know.  Stan, Boris and I have been pretty "
"insular.  I guess we'd better get to know some of the others here "
"eventually.\"  He looks around the room, his eyes dull.  \"It feels it "
"should be a temporary stop, but it's starting to look like we'll be here for"
" the long term.  If we live that long."
msgstr ""
"ピリピリしているが、詳しくは知らない。スタンとボリスと私の3人で固まっているからね。他の人達とも交流した方が良いとは思っているんだ。」彼はぼんやりと室内を見渡しました。「センターでの滞在は一時的なものだと思っていたが、もっと長い時間を過ごすことになるかな。まぁ、長生きできればの話だけど。"

#. ~ Unique name of a male NPC
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Guneet_Singh.json
msgid "Guneet Singh"
msgstr "ｸﾞﾆｰﾄ ｼﾝ"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Guneet_Singh.json
msgid ""
"*is a young man in a white turban, surprisingly clean compared to the rest "
"of his outfit.  He turns from the window as you approach, then raises his "
"eyebrows when he sees you're a new face.  \"Oh, hello.  I don't think I've "
"seen you around before.  I'm Guneet, people call me Gunny.\""
msgstr ""
"*は窓の向こうを見ている若い男性です。頭に巻いている白いターバンは、他の着衣と比べて驚くほど汚れていません。彼はこちらを振り返り、少し驚いたようです。「あっ、こんにちは。初めて会う人だ。僕はグニート、ガニーって呼んで。」"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Guneet_Singh.json
msgid "Nice to meet you, Gunny."
msgstr "はじめまして、ガニー。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Guneet_Singh.json
msgid "Hi Gunny, nice to meet you.  I gotta go though."
msgstr "やぁガニー、ごきげんよう。悪いけどもう行くよ。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Guneet_Singh.json
msgid "*turns away from the window, noticing you coming close.  \""
msgstr "*は外の景色を眺めるのを止め、こちらに振り返りました。「"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Guneet_Singh.json
msgid "Hi, Gunny.  What's up?"
msgstr "やあ、ガニー。調子はどう？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Guneet_Singh.json
msgid "Hi Gunny.  I can't stay to talk."
msgstr "やあガニー。話は後にしよう。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Guneet_Singh.json
msgid ""
"I guess we're still doing that stuff?  Cool.  Nice to meet you too.  What's "
"up?"
msgstr "生きてる人が外にもいるんだ？よかった。はじめまして。どうしたの？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Guneet_Singh.json
msgid ""
"What's up?\"  He stares at you for a moment.  \"What a weird question.  The "
"world ended.  That's what's up.  What am I supposed to answer to that one?"
msgstr ""
"調子はどう、だって？」彼は一瞬、こちらを凝視しました。「変なこと聞くなよ。世界が終わったってのに、調子も何もないよ。一体どう答えろっていうんだ？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Guneet_Singh.json
msgid ""
"I was in high school, you know.\"  Gunny jabs his thumb at his shirt, which "
"reads 'Alexander Bullock High'.  \"Most of the way through my junior year.  "
"'My story'?  I got on a bus with my parents, the bus crashed, and everyone "
"died except a few people, most of whom are crammed into this little shelter "
"now.  Who knows when we're getting out."
msgstr ""
"見ての通り、僕は高校生。」ガニーは「アレクサンダー・ブロック高校」とプリントされたシャツを親指で示しました。「もうすぐ2年生が終わるって頃だね。それで、話が聞きたいって？両親と乗り込んだバスが事故って、ほとんど全員が死んだ。生き残りの大半はこの小さな避難所に詰め込まれてる。いつになったら出られるんだろうな。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Guneet_Singh.json
msgid "Your family all made it here?"
msgstr "あなたの家族もここにいるのか？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Guneet_Singh.json
msgid ""
"Yeah, we did.\"  He gestures to a turbaned older man, speaking quietly with "
"a small woman a little way away.  \"Seems like it should be a great thing, "
"right?  It is.  We're super lucky.  But I can't help feel like people blame "
"us for it.  I keep wondering, y'know, 'why us'.  What makes me so special?  "
"And how can I even enjoy this, when everyone around me is hurting so bad?"
msgstr ""
"ああ、そうだよ。」少し離れたところにいるターバンを巻いた年配の男性を、彼は指し示しました。男性は小柄な女性と小声で話をしているようです。「本当に良かったって思うだろ？その通り。僕らは超ラッキーなんだ。でも、幸運を恨まれてるような気がしてならない。『どうして僕らが』って、ずっと考えてる。どうして僕らが特別に助かったんだ？周りが皆傷ついているのに、どうして喜べるんだ？ってね。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Guneet_Singh.json
msgid "Is there something you could do to help the others?"
msgstr "他の人たちの助けになることをしてみてはどうだろう？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Guneet_Singh.json
msgid ""
"*shrugs.  \"I don't have any skills.  I'm just a kid.  What am I going to "
"do?\"  Before you can answer, he shakes his head.  \"I'm being pathetic, "
"sorry.  You're right, I should see if there's something I can give back to "
"the community, maybe make my place in it.  That's a good call.\"  He "
"scratches his chin and looks out a gap in the shutters on the window.  "
"\"Thanks.\""
msgstr ""
"*は肩をすくめました。「何もできないよ。僕はただのガキだ。何をしろって言うのさ？」こちらが返答する前に、彼は首を振って制しました。「情けないな、ごめん。あなたの言うとおりだ。何かコミュニティに恩返しして、自分の居場所を作れないか、考えてみるよ。きっとそれがいい。」ガニーは顎を掻きながら、窓のシャッターの隙間から外の景色を眺めました。「アドバイスありがとう。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Guneet_Singh.json
msgid "It sucks in here, there's no two ways about it"
msgstr "ここは最悪だ。どうしようもない"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Guneet_Singh.json
msgid ""
".  Still, we're starting to find a bit of a place for ourselves.  I've been "
"hanging out with Aleesha a bit, I didn't used to think we'd have a lot in "
"common but there's more than you'd think.  My mom and dad are starting to "
"relax a little too."
msgstr ""
"。それでも、自分たちの居場所を少しずつ見つけられてる気がするよ。アリーシャとは結構話すんだ。そんなに共通の話題もないと思ってたけど、実際話すと意外と気が合ってね。両親も、少しはリラックスできるようになったっぽい。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Guneet_Singh.json
msgid ""
".  People don't talk to us because we wear turbans and we still have each "
"other.  They think because we're still together, we didn't lose anything.  "
"My dad believes it, too, and I think my mom's on the fence."
msgstr ""
"。ターバンを巻いて家族だけで固まってる僕らには、誰も話しかけようとしない。家族が一緒なら別に問題ないだろって思われてる。父さんも同じ考え。母さんも、多分同じだろうな。"

#. ~ Unique name of a female NPC
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
msgid "Jenny Forcette"
msgstr "ｼﾞｪﾆｰ ﾌｫｾｯﾃ"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
msgid "What are you working on?"
msgstr "どんな仕事を任されているんだ？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
msgid "How's everything going with that defense system?"
msgstr "防衛システムの調子はどう？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
msgid "Tell me a bit about your background."
msgstr "あなたは以前どんな職に就いていたんだ？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
msgid "Are you free to teach me anything today?"
msgstr "私に何か技術を教えてくれないか？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
msgid "Can you tell me anything about the other refugees here?"
msgstr "ここにいる他の避難者について教えてもらえないか？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
msgid "How did you make it here during the chaos?"
msgstr "この混乱の中、どうやってここまで来たんだ？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Uyen_Tran.json
msgid "What do you think happened to the world?"
msgstr "この世界に何が起こったと思う？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
msgid ""
"*is a thin woman in her early thirties, with the sort of pale, freckled skin"
" that looks like it would burn if she thought too hard about the sun.  Her "
"clothes and bearing suggest she might once have been carefully put-together,"
" but she now has the harried look of someone with too many worries and too "
"little sleep.  She looks up from a laptop and smiles as you approach.  \"Hi "
"there.  Haven't see you around here before.  I'm Jenny, Jenny Forcette.\""
msgstr ""
"*は30代前半の、痩せ身の女性です。肌はそばかすだらけで、日光に当たれば燃え尽きてしまいそうなほど青白い肌をしています。服装や立ち居振る舞いを見ると、かつては上品な人物だったように思えますが、今は心配事や焦りで押し潰されそうな、寝不足の顔つきになっています。彼女はノートパソコンから顔を上げ、微笑みました。「どうも。初めましてかな。私はジェニー、ジェニー・フォセッテ。」"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
msgid "Nice meeting you.  What are you doing on that computer?"
msgstr "初めまして。ノートPCで何をしているんだ？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
msgid "Nice meeting you.  I'd best get going, though."
msgstr "初めまして。もうそろそろ行かないと。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
msgid ""
"*looks up from her computer and gives you a quick, thin smile.  \"Hello "
"again.\""
msgstr "*はパソコンから素早く顔を上げ、軽く微笑みました。「どうも、また会ったね。」"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
msgid ""
"*tips the lid of her laptop closed and looks up.  \"Nice to see you again.\""
msgstr "*はノートパソコンの蓋を閉じ、こちらを見ました。「また会えて嬉しいわ。」"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
msgid "Hi, Jenny.  What are you up to these days?"
msgstr "やあ、ジェニー。最近どう？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
msgid "Sorry Jenny, I can't stay to chat."
msgstr "悪いねジェニー、話している暇はないんだ。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
msgid ""
"I'm puttering around, I always have stuff on the go.\"  Jenny rubs the "
"bridge of her nose briefly, blinking fatigue from her eyes.  \"Gotta keep "
"busy, keep my mind off stuff, you know?"
msgstr ""
"適当に弄ってるだけ。PCはいつも手元に置いてる。」ジェニーは鼻の下を軽くこすり、疲れた目を何度か瞬かせました。「とにかく忙しくしてないと落ち着かない気持ち、分かるでしょ？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
msgid ""
"Me?  I trained at MIT in mechanical engineering, I worked for a long time as"
" senior engineer at Marduk Thermal in Rhode Island.  It was a good job, but "
"I landed my dream gig at Boston Dynamics and moved up north to start "
"there.\"  She tips back her head and lets out a long, wistful sigh.  \"I had"
" just finished my orientation and was going to start work when the riots "
"started.  Just my damn luck."
msgstr ""
"私？MITで機械工学の勉強をして、ロードアイランド州のマーダック・ターミナル社で上級エンジニアとしてしばらく働いてた。いい職場だったけど、夢を実現するためボストン・ダイナミクスに転職して、心機一転、北上してきたの。」彼女は天を仰ぎ、長い溜息をつきました。「ちょうどオリエンテーションが終わって、さあ仕事を始めるぞって時に暴動が始まってね。運が悪すぎでしょ。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
msgid "That's impressive, but there must be more to you than just your job."
msgstr "大変だったな。仕事以外にも生き甲斐が見つかるといいのだけれど。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
msgid "You must know some great stuff.  Can you teach me anything?"
msgstr "きっと色々な知識を持っているんだろうな。何か教えてもらえないか？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
msgid ""
"So, did anyone tell you there are actual no-kidding talking cyborg-robot "
"people out there now?"
msgstr "そう言えば、これは真面目な話なんだけど、話ができるサイボーグだかロボットだかの存在を、聞いたことはある？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
msgid "Sorry about your luck.  What were you saying before?"
msgstr "それは不運だったな。前の話をもう一度してもらえるか？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
msgid ""
"*grins and tugs at her shirt, an uncharacteristically crisp white T-shirt "
"sporting a brightly colored penguin holding a slide rule, and a rainbow "
"slogan reading 'sudo build it the way I told you to'.  \"Ha!  You must not "
"know many engineers, hey?  I guess there's more to me than engineering, but "
"most of my hobbies come back to it one way or the other.  It's not that I "
"live for my work, doing engineering for a heating company wasn't some great "
"dream, but when I got home I'd putter with the projects I wanted to do "
"instead of the ones they made me do.  You know?  And of course, I had my "
"friends and things, we'd go out or hang out and play board games and stuff."
"  Maybe some day I'll get a board game group started up here, although "
"there's nothing wrong with the card games we've got now.  Plus I don't think"
" Zombicide would hold the same interest for me as it used to.\""
msgstr ""
"*はにっこり笑い、着ているTシャツを見せびらかしました。計算尺をもった色鮮やかなペンギンと、虹色の『ちゃんと言ったとおりにsudoをビルドしなさい』というスローガンがプリントされています。「ハッ！エンジニアの知り合いが居ないの？私の趣味には大抵何らかの形で工学が関わってる。仕事のために生きてる訳じゃないし、空調の会社で働くことが一番の夢でもなかったけど、家に帰れば仕事と関係ない自分のプロジェクトに没頭できる。理想的でしょ？もちろん、友達もいたし、遊びに行ったり、ボードゲームをやるのも楽しかった。今ここで流行ってるトランプゲームもいいけど、いつかボードゲーム同好会を立ち上げたいね。でも、ゾンビ対人間で戦うゲームはもう前みたいに楽しく遊べないだろうな。」"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
msgid "What kind of board games do you play?"
msgstr "どんなボードゲームで遊ぶんだ？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
msgid ""
"*shrugs, looking distant.  \"I don't really like to talk about that time "
"much.  None of us do.  Short story is that I made it to one of the "
"evacuation shelters and got loaded onto a bus.  It was supposed to go to "
"some sort of FEMA support camp, but there was a roadblock on the way there."
"  A few people just jumped out and ran for the military for protection.  "
"They… it… it was bad.  The driver managed to get us turned around and booked"
" it, and I guess they didn't chase us.  She took us back to one of the "
"shelters and we found the address for this place.  Only a few of us decided "
"to risk it, the rest stayed at the shelter to try their luck a different "
"way.  I still wonder how they did.\""
msgstr ""
"*は肩をすくめ、遠くを見つめました。「あのときのことは、あまり話したくない。みんなそうだよ。簡単に言うと、私は避難所の一つに辿り着いて、バスに乗せられた。FEMAが支援してるキャンプに行く予定だったけど、途中で襲撃されてね。何人かが立ち向かうべきだと言って、外に飛び出した。あの人たちは...本当...気の毒に。運転手さんが何とか皆を諫めて、大急ぎで引き返したから、追いかけては来なかった。彼女はその後も避難所の一つに引き返して、ここの住所を調べてくれた。でも、危険を冒してセンターに向かおうと決めたのは私ふくめほんの数人。他の人たちは、運試しならこっちの方がマシだと言って、避難所に残ったんだ。みんな、今は何をしてるんだろうね。」"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
msgid ""
"Ha!  I wonder how long that's going to be one of our go-to small talk "
"questions.  It's perfect, isn't it?  Doesn't make you talk about the worst "
"stuff but stays on theme for what's on everyone's mind.  Okay, I'll bite.  "
"Have you heard any of the really wild stories?  Giant monsters the size of "
"skyscrapers kicking over tanks and stuff, during the worst days?  I think "
"somehow our planet got moved into another dimension, probably some kind of "
"experimental process gone wrong.  During transit, some of those things came "
"across, but they left when we arrived wherever we are now.  The rules are "
"different here, and maybe we're superimposed with whatever version of Earth "
"was here to start with, and that's why we hear about aliens and other "
"unbelievable stuff out there along with the zombies.\"  She grins.  \"And "
"before you say that's implausible, bear in mind that *the dead walk now*, so"
" plausibility is off the table."
msgstr ""
"ハハ！雑談の定番ネタといったら、やっぱりそれだよね。最高だと思わない？酷い思い出を語るより、誰もが想像してる物語を話す方がずっといい。よし、その話に乗ったよ。これだけ突飛な説は聞いたこと無いんじゃない？これから先、超高層ビルサイズの巨大モンスターが現れて戦車すら蹴散らしちゃう？ううん、そんなもんじゃないよ。どこかで何かの実験が失敗して、私たちの惑星は何故か別次元に転移したんだ。移動中に巨大モンスターがいる世界も通ったかもしれないけど、通り過ぎたんだろうね。今は色々な法則がおかしくなってる。きっと私たちは、元からここにあった別次元の地球と重なったんだ。だから、ゾンビ以外にも、宇宙人とか信じられないものの噂を聞くことになるんだよ。」彼女は笑いながら語りました。「とんでもない話だけど、*死者が歩く世界*なんだから、もっともらしさなんて考えなくていいじゃん。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
msgid ""
"*lets out a low whistle.  \"No, not as such.  I've heard some rumors, I "
"guess, but nothing credible.\"  She pauses, looking thoughtful.  \"I think, "
"unless you can offer me some detailed answers about who and what they are "
"and how they work, you'd better not tell me anything else.  I don't know if "
"I could handle the stress.\"  With a gulp, she pulls listlessly at her "
"earlobe.  \"If you do really know some juicy tidbits though, spill.\""
msgstr ""
"*は低い口笛を鳴らしました。「いいえ、有り得ない。噂は聞いた気がするけど、信ぴょう性はないね。」そこまで言うと、思慮深い表情で言葉を続けます。「そのロボが何者か、何が目的か、どうやって動いてるのか、その辺を詳しく答えてもらえないなら、この話は打ち切った方がいい。私がストレスに耐えられないもの。」そこまで一気にまくし立てると、気怠そうに耳たぶを弄り始めました。「本当に興味深い話があるんだったら、ぜひ教えてほしいものね。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
msgid ""
"Well, I know they're cyborgs, from some other dimension.  I think they're "
"humans underneath the machines though.  Some of them kinda speak English."
msgstr "そうだな、そいつは別次元からやってきたサイボーグだってことは分かっている。でも、機械の裏に人間が入ってるのかも。言葉が通じる奴もいた。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
msgid ""
"*puts her hands on her hips and glares at you.  \"I thought I made it clear "
"I wasn't willing to accept enticing tidbits of information.  What the actual"
" fuck?  Interdimensional cyborgs?  I don't want to believe you, but also, I "
"already kinda thought there might be some multidimensional hijinks going on "
"here, so I kinda do want to believe you.  They speak English though?  Are "
"you sure this isn't some kind of scam?  Are you just fucking with me?  "
"Honestly this would be a great way to fuck with me.\""
msgstr ""
"*は腰に手を当て、こちらを睨みました。「面白そうなネタは止めてって言ったと思うんだけどな。それで、一体何ですって？別次元のサイボーグ？信じたくもないけど、この世界で多次元的な何かが悪さしてるって説は考えたことがあったから、ちょっと信じちゃいそう。それで、言葉が通じるって？何かの詐欺じゃないの？私のことカモにしようとしてる？正直言って、私を引っ掛けるつもりなら最高に効果的なやり口だと思う。」"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
msgid "[Show her your bionic interface.]"
msgstr "[移植したCBMを見せる]"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
msgid ""
"*breathes a long, sighing curse as she examines your CBM interface.  "
"\"Holeeeeeeshiiiiiiit.  This is amazing!  Like seriously, it's not even high"
" tech.  At least not this part.  Can I see the schematics?  Can we dissect "
"you?  I'm kidding.  Unless?  No, really kidding though.  Holy shit.\"  She "
"pauses and studies you with a furrowed brow.  \"Wait, you let a strange "
"interdimensional cyborg do brain surgery on you?  Never mind, I'd totally do"
" that too.  Can you get me one of these?  No, I'd wind up taking it out and "
"dismantling it.\"  She looks you up and down.  \"Thanks.  That's incredible."
"  It sucks that the world ended but I'm glad to know at least it ended with "
"*cyborgs*.\""
msgstr ""
"*はCBMインターフェイスをじっくり眺めて長い溜息をつき、感情に任せて言葉を吐き出しました。「ホオォォリイィィシイィット。これ、すごい！マジ、ハイテックなんてもんじゃない。少なくともこの部品はね。回路を見せてくれない？というか、解剖していい？冗談だよ。いや、冗談じゃないかも？ううん、本当に冗談。何てこと。」彼女は微動だにせず、眉間にしわを寄せて観察を続けています。「待って、あなた、よく分からない別次元のサイボーグに脳の手術を任せたの？いえ問題ないよ、私も絶対そうしたから。私にも移植してもらえたりしない？ああ、でも結局取り除いて分解してみないとダメだな。」こちらの身体を上から下まで見回しています。「ありがとう。信じられない。世界が終わりを迎えたのは残念だけど、少なくともゴールが*サイボーグ*だと知れたのは嬉しいね。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
msgid ""
"*scrunches her face in thought for a moment.  \"There was a whole world out "
"there of weird board games for ultra nerdy people.  Lots of that stuff never"
" really reached mainstream.  One of the hardest parts of evacuating for me "
"was leaving my garage full of esoteric crowdfunded games I've never "
"played.\""
msgstr ""
"*は一瞬、難しい顔で考え込みました。「超ニッチなオタク向けキワモノボードゲームって言うのかな。大抵はメインストリームから外れてるような奴だね。避難するとき一番辛かったのは、まだ手も付けてないクラウドファンディングの変なゲーム類を全部ガレージに置きっぱなしにしてきたこと。」"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
msgid "Have you ever thought about going back for them?"
msgstr "まさか、取りに帰ろうと思っているとか？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
msgid "Do you mean stuff like D&D?"
msgstr "ダンジョンズ&ドラゴンズとか、そういうゲームだろうか？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
msgid ""
"No, mainly because my whole neighborhood burnt to the ground.  Some scouts "
"went by a while ago.  Nothing there for me but melted plastic miniatures and"
" thousands of hours of gameplay I'll never have."
msgstr ""
"いいえ、近所一帯が焼けちゃってたからね。少し前に偵察に行ったんだ。溶けたプラスチック製のミニチュアたちと何千時間もの思い出以外、何も残ってない。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
msgid ""
"Well, of course I played the mandatory amount of dice based RPGs necessary "
"to graduate my engineering program,\" she grins.  \"They're fun, something "
"like that would be nice around here, but I'm not that kind of storyteller "
"and I don't think anyone else here is nerdy enough for it.\"  Jenny tips her"
" head a bit.  \"It's nice that you're asking but don't worry about me, I've "
"got recreation.\""
msgstr ""
"もちろん、機械工学科の必修科目だし、ダイスを振るタイプのRPGはたくさんプレイしたね。」ジェニーはニヤリと笑いました。「でも、私は語り部ってタイプじゃないし、センター内にもそういうのが得意な人はいなさそう。」彼女は少し首を傾げました。「話を色々聞いてくれるのは嬉しいけど、心配しないで。暇つぶしは自分で用意できるから。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
msgid "Have you ever thought about going back for your board games?"
msgstr "ボードゲームを家に取りに戻ろうと思ったことは？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
msgid ""
"Huh.\"  She purses her lips and looks at you reluctantly.  \"I guess I can "
"teach you a bit, but you'd have to be like, my on-the-job apprentice and "
"help me get stuff done.  It'll cost you a bit depending on what you want to "
"learn.  Do you know anything about electronics, computers, or mechanics "
"already?\""
msgstr ""
"うーん。」彼女は口をへの字に曲げ、渋い顔でこちらを見ました。「少しなら教えられるけど、実習生ってことで、色々手伝ってもらうよ。何を学びたいかにもよるけど、多少は費用も取るからね。電子工学やコンピュータ、機械整備の知識はある？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
msgid "[Skill 2] I'm not a total noob."
msgstr "[関連スキル 2] まったくの初心者ではない。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
msgid "[Skill <2] No, that's why I want you to teach me."
msgstr "[関連スキル 2未満] いいや、だから教えてほしいんだ。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
msgid "[INT 10] No, but I'm a fast learner."
msgstr "[知性 10] いいや、でも飲み込みは早い方だ。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
msgid "Um, you know what?  Nevermind.  What were you saying?"
msgstr "ええと、何だって？いや、前の話をもう一度聞かせてくれる？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
msgid ""
"All right, fine.\"  Jenny sets aside the computer and gets up.  \"Grab some "
"tools and do as I tell you."
msgstr "よし、分かった。」ジェニーはパソコンを脇に置き、立ち上がりました。「じゃあ工具を持って、言うとおりにやってみて。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
msgid "Just say the word, teach."
msgstr "よし、準備できた。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
msgid "Actually, I'd better get going.  Let's do this later."
msgstr "実は、今から用事があるんだ。また今度にしよう。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
msgid ""
"&\"I'm sorry, I don't have the time to teach someone who can't pull their "
"weight, I just don't.\"  She gives you a look of genuine regret, then "
"shrugs."
msgstr "悪いんだけど、基礎的な内容も分からないとなると、私ではお手上げだよ。」彼女は心から落胆したように、肩をすくめました。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
msgid "Fine.  What were you saying?"
msgstr "分かった。さっきの話をもう一度聞かせて？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
msgid ""
"Well, thanks to your help, I've been designing some turrets that would use a"
" central air system to power pneumatic rifle turrets around the center.  "
"It's a lot easier than trying to make gunpowder!\"  She shrugs quickly.  "
"\"I'm probably getting ahead of myself here, I don't think we're due to run "
"out of gunpowder for years, but I also think the design is quieter and more "
"long-term extendable."
msgstr ""
"ええ、おかげさまで、センターの周りに並べる空圧式ライフルタレット用の圧力制御システムの設計が順調に進んでるよ。これなら火薬を作るよりずっと簡単じゃない？」彼女はすぐに肩をすくめました。「ま、火薬が枯渇するのは何年も先の話だけど。でも、こっちの方が発砲音は静かだし、長期的な拡張にも適してると思うんだよね。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
msgid ""
"About a month ago, I got a mold for making high-caliber air rifle bullets.  "
"I've been designing some turrets that would use a central air system to "
"power pneumatic rifle turrets around the center.  It's a lot easier than "
"trying to make gunpowder!\"  She shrugs quickly.  \"I'm probably getting "
"ahead of myself here, I don't think we're due to run out of gunpowder for "
"years, but I also think the design is quieter and more long-term extendable."
msgstr ""
"1か月くらい前に、空圧式ライフルに使う大口径弾の金型を手に入れたんだ。ここ最近は、センターの周りに並べる空圧式ライフルタレット用の圧力制御システムの設計に取り掛かってる。火薬を作るよりずっと簡単だよ！」彼女はすぐに肩をすくめました。「ま、火薬が枯渇するのは何年も先の話だけど。でも、こっちの方が発砲音が静かだし、長期的な拡張にも適してると思うんだよね。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
msgid ""
"I recently came into possession of this mold for making high-caliber air "
"rifle bullets.  I'm kinda working on a design that would use them to protect"
" the base.  Got a long way to go, though.  If you happen to see anything in "
"your travels about high-powered air rifles, it would help a lot."
msgstr ""
"最近、空圧ライフルに使う大口径弾の金型を入手したんだ。それを使って、拠点防衛のデザインを考えてるところ。長い道のりになりそうだよ。もし、旅先で高威力の空圧ライフルに関係しそうな情報を見つけたら、ぜひ教えてほしい。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
msgid ""
"If I see anything, I'll let you know.  Can you tell me more about your "
"project?"
msgstr "何かあったら知らせよう。その計画について詳しく教えてもらえる？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
msgid "Tell me more about your project."
msgstr "ここで進めているプロジェクトについて詳しく知りたい。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/CleverRaven/Cataclysm-
#. DDA/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
msgctxt "u:f"
msgid ""
"&\"Holy shit, what are the odds?  OK, stand back and hold on.\"  Jenny "
"begins peppering you with questions, which you answer to the best of your "
"ability.  She seems quite satisfied.  \"Well, I can't thank you enough,\" "
"she smiles after a few minutes.  \"You probably just saved me weeks of "
"reinventing the wheel.  Here, it's not much but it's all I've got.\"  She "
"hands you a bundle of the local currency."
msgstr ""
"&「嘘でしょ、そんな偶然ある？オーケー、ちょっと待って。」投げかけられた質問にできる限り答えると、ジェニーはおおむね満足したようです。「もう、本当に、感謝してもしきれないね。」質疑応答が終わり、彼女はにっこり笑いました。「これで、車輪の再発明で無駄にする筈だった時間を節約できたわけだ。これ、少ないけど、受け取って。」彼女はセンター内で使われている通貨の束を手渡しました。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/CleverRaven/Cataclysm-
#. DDA/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
